WEBVTT

1
00:01:48.695 --> 00:01:52.032
NARRATOR: With over a million casualties
from the Battle of Verdun alone,

2
00:01:51.906 --> 00:01:54.409
the death toll continues to climb.

3
00:01:56.494 --> 00:01:59.330
Never before has the battlefield
been so vast

4
00:01:59.330 --> 00:02:02.751
and never before has the fighting
been so gruesome.

5
00:02:03.293 --> 00:02:05.670
Whether on the ground
in brutal trench warfare

6
00:02:05.670 --> 00:02:08.298
or high, high in the skies above them,

7
00:02:08.173 --> 00:02:12.594
millions of young soldiers continue to die
with no end in sight.

8
00:02:14.012 --> 00:02:17.891
It seems as though the German aggressors
cannot be stopped as the Allied nations

9
00:02:17.891 --> 00:02:20.101
valiantly fight to survive.

10
00:02:21.227 --> 00:02:23.730
The Great War rages on.

11
00:02:29.777 --> 00:02:31.446
Hello, Blaine.

12
00:02:31.446 --> 00:02:34.157
You're not gonna give me any problems,
are you?

13
00:02:34.782 --> 00:02:38.202
Got no quarrel with you. Just that banker.

14
00:02:38.953 --> 00:02:43.124
You broke up Sandford's face pretty good.
He's looking to see you in jail.

15
00:02:43.416 --> 00:02:45.126
He had it coming.

16
00:02:46.794 --> 00:02:49.046
I got a bench warrant for your arrest.

17
00:02:49.046 --> 00:02:51.883
I'm gonna give you half an hour
before I serve it.

18
00:02:51.883 --> 00:02:56.137
If I were you, I'd get out of town.
Way out of town.

19
00:02:56.804 --> 00:03:00.558
NARRATOR: Fear continues to grow that
without the United States' intervention,

20
00:03:00.433 --> 00:03:02.310
France could soon fall.

21
00:03:02.310 --> 00:03:05.146
Despite President Wilson's refusal
to enter the conflict,

22
00:03:05.146 --> 00:03:09.817
some determined young Americans
have volunteered to join the fray anyway.

23
00:03:09.817 --> 00:03:12.111
Using the latest in flying war machines,

24
00:03:12.111 --> 00:03:16.699
the French have created a new
airborne combat unit just for these Yanks.

25
00:03:19.201 --> 00:03:22.246
From all over,
American boys are making their way

26
00:03:22.246 --> 00:03:26.083
across the Atlantic to learn how to fly.

27
00:03:35.593 --> 00:03:36.844
Good luck, son.

28
00:03:36.844 --> 00:03:39.430
I'll try to bring home a couple of medals
like you and Grandpa.

29
00:03:39.430 --> 00:03:41.307
We'll march together
in the 4th of July parade,

30
00:03:41.307 --> 00:03:42.766
you'll see.

31
00:03:42.975 --> 00:03:44.351
(SNIFFLING)

32
00:03:44.351 --> 00:03:47.021
Don't worry, Mom. I got the Jensen blood.

33
00:03:47.146 --> 00:03:50.691
Haven't made the bullet yet
that's stronger than that.

34
00:03:54.236 --> 00:03:58.407
I'm gonna miss you so much.
Write me every day, okay?

35
00:03:59.116 --> 00:04:00.701
CONDUCTOR: All aboard!

36
00:04:02.995 --> 00:04:04.246
I will.

37
00:04:15.924 --> 00:04:18.969
I'll be fine. Don't worry.

38
00:04:20.095 --> 00:04:21.888
I love you, Laura.

39
00:04:38.029 --> 00:04:39.281
(BELL RINGING)

40
00:04:39.364 --> 00:04:41.158
(SPEAKING FRENCH)

41
00:05:21.406 --> 00:05:23.908
I'm gonna learn to fly airplanes.

42
00:05:27.453 --> 00:05:28.913
SAILOR: Come on, now.

43
00:05:34.877 --> 00:05:35.920
(WOMAN LAUGHING)

44
00:05:35.920 --> 00:05:37.046
Thank you so much.

45
00:05:37.130 --> 00:05:39.340
- Please take great care of them.
- Yes, sir.

46
00:05:41.926 --> 00:05:45.888
Well, you should have
everything you need.

47
00:05:46.013 --> 00:05:47.682
Thank you, Father.

48
00:05:47.807 --> 00:05:51.144
I've made arrangements
to come to Paris in the fall.

49
00:05:51.018 --> 00:05:54.147
- I may come and see you then.
- Yes, Father.

50
00:05:54.981 --> 00:05:56.732
Buck up, my boy.

51
00:05:57.275 --> 00:05:59.986
This noble conflict you're about to enter

52
00:05:59.986 --> 00:06:03.739
is the kind of adventure
that can set one above the herd.

53
00:06:04.073 --> 00:06:05.074
I suppose so.

54
00:06:05.074 --> 00:06:08.661
Damn it, Briggs, have you no enthusiasm
for anything that might distinguish you?

55
00:06:08.661 --> 00:06:10.746
It's quite enough
you've been dismissed from Harvard,

56
00:06:10.746 --> 00:06:16.669
but your continuing lack of direction
has become an embarrassment.

57
00:06:16.585 --> 00:06:19.672
It's time to do something
worthy of your name.

58
00:06:21.173 --> 00:06:23.259
Have you nothing to say?

59
00:06:24.510 --> 00:06:25.845
No, Father.

60
00:06:43.028 --> 00:06:44.280
(BELL CLANGING)

61
00:06:48.701 --> 00:06:50.661
(PEOPLE CHATTERING)

62
00:06:58.168 --> 00:07:02.214
They said we're supposed to go
to a place on 228 Rue Brion.

63
00:07:02.131 --> 00:07:03.799
That's where we can buy
all our aviator clothes.

64
00:07:03.799 --> 00:07:05.884
I can't understand a word on this map.

65
00:07:05.968 --> 00:07:09.012
Hello? Does anybody here speak English?

66
00:07:08.887 --> 00:07:10.556
(SPEAKING FRENCH)

67
00:07:10.806 --> 00:07:12.057
Okay.

68
00:07:12.891 --> 00:07:15.143
Brion. Rue Brion.

69
00:07:17.896 --> 00:07:19.565
(WHISTLE SOUNDING)

70
00:07:24.444 --> 00:07:25.988
Right there. Yeah.

71
00:07:26.405 --> 00:07:27.990
Rue Brion. Do you see it?

72
00:07:28.073 --> 00:07:30.575
Excuse me, sir? We're a little lost, and...

73
00:07:30.575 --> 00:07:32.160
(SPEAKS FRENCH)

74
00:07:32.911 --> 00:07:34.329
Never mind.

75
00:07:34.329 --> 00:07:35.831
(URINATING)

76
00:07:36.832 --> 00:07:38.625
Oh, good Lord.

77
00:07:56.768 --> 00:07:58.436
(SPEAKING FRENCH)

78
00:08:02.399 --> 00:08:04.192
(SPEAKING FRENCH)

79
00:08:22.961 --> 00:08:25.964
On your right,
you've got the English squadron.

80
00:08:25.964 --> 00:08:29.634
They fly the Bristol, the Sopwith
and the SE5As.

81
00:08:29.509 --> 00:08:31.594
- This place is really something.
- Have you ever seen anything...

82
00:08:31.594 --> 00:08:34.097
And here is the French detachment.

83
00:08:34.931 --> 00:08:37.016
They fly Nieuport 11s.

84
00:08:45.483 --> 00:08:47.235
(THENAULT SPEAKING FRENCH)

85
00:09:08.422 --> 00:09:10.675
How many of you speak French?

86
00:09:12.051 --> 00:09:13.427
(GIROUX SPEAKING FRENCH)

87
00:09:21.644 --> 00:09:26.107
Our country has been at war since
we were first attacked three years ago,

88
00:09:26.107 --> 00:09:29.860
and we have lost more than a million
of our young men.

89
00:09:29.860 --> 00:09:31.153
(MEN SHOUTING)

90
00:09:31.153 --> 00:09:34.698
Your country turned its back
on this conflict,

91
00:09:35.199 --> 00:09:40.538
but you have bravely volunteered
to join the fight to preserve freedom.

92
00:09:40.621 --> 00:09:45.834
All right, there is not much more to see,
so let's have eyes forward.

93
00:09:48.545 --> 00:09:50.839
We do not expect you to win the war,

94
00:09:50.965 --> 00:09:55.135
only to do what your conscience
commands and your courage allows.

95
00:09:56.053 --> 00:09:59.473
You will train for two months,
then we'll see which one of you

96
00:09:59.473 --> 00:10:02.935
becomes your squadron's first ace.

97
00:10:02.810 --> 00:10:04.395
That'll be me.

98
00:10:09.191 --> 00:10:11.819
- Who are you?
- Blaine Rawlings.

99
00:10:11.819 --> 00:10:14.488
We arrive in uniform, Mr. Rawlings.

100
00:10:15.322 --> 00:10:19.326
Yeah, I wasn't quite sure
how it all went together.

101
00:10:19.201 --> 00:10:20.452
(SNICKERING)

102
00:10:20.577 --> 00:10:21.912
I see.

103
00:10:21.912 --> 00:10:24.498
So these are the new corpses, huh?

104
00:10:25.874 --> 00:10:27.334
What's this?

105
00:10:27.334 --> 00:10:29.544
We got cowpunchers coming over now?

106
00:10:29.628 --> 00:10:31.171
Yeah, I done some cowboying.

107
00:10:31.171 --> 00:10:33.382
You think a six-shooter's
gonna help you up there?

108
00:10:33.507 --> 00:10:37.427
Well, whatever you were using
didn't seem to do you much good.

109
00:10:38.178 --> 00:10:39.846
He's funny.

110
00:10:39.846 --> 00:10:42.265
I may even come to his funeral.

111
00:10:43.266 --> 00:10:47.437
The Captain bother to tell you
the life expectancy for pilots around here?

112
00:10:47.354 --> 00:10:49.231
It's three to six weeks.

113
00:10:50.273 --> 00:10:55.070
Let me guess, you're here because
you thought it'd be fun to fly airplanes.

114
00:10:57.989 --> 00:11:00.200
Go home while you still can.

115
00:11:01.618 --> 00:11:04.537
Guy sure knows how to make friends.

116
00:11:04.663 --> 00:11:06.748
All his friends are dead.

117
00:11:12.796 --> 00:11:14.381
(SPEAKS FRENCH)

118
00:11:21.346 --> 00:11:22.806
We're here.

119
00:11:23.640 --> 00:11:25.225
There we are.

120
00:11:25.517 --> 00:11:27.477
(SPEAKS FRENCH)

121
00:11:29.145 --> 00:11:31.147
This is your quarters.

122
00:11:31.564 --> 00:11:32.607
(WHISTLES)

123
00:11:32.732 --> 00:11:36.236
Soon others from your country
will stay here as well.

124
00:11:38.571 --> 00:11:41.157
I've never seen anything like this
back home. Have you?

125
00:11:41.157 --> 00:11:43.326
As a matter of fact, I have.

126
00:11:44.410 --> 00:11:46.996
Beats the hell out of the infantry.

127
00:11:47.914 --> 00:11:49.916
Frenchies sure put on a nice war.

128
00:11:49.916 --> 00:11:50.958
(CHUCKLING)

129
00:11:59.425 --> 00:12:01.677
- Home sweet home.
- SKINNER: My, oh, my.

130
00:12:02.762 --> 00:12:04.096
(CHUCKLES)

131
00:12:09.101 --> 00:12:11.938
- Careful, you oaf!
- Hey, I'm sorry.

132
00:12:12.438 --> 00:12:16.817
That's a 100-year-old bottle of cognac.
It's worth more than you are.

133
00:12:16.692 --> 00:12:17.860
Nice.

134
00:12:17.944 --> 00:12:21.948
Your benefactor, William K. Vanderbilt,
has rented this château for you.

135
00:12:23.074 --> 00:12:24.200
(ROARING)

136
00:12:24.200 --> 00:12:25.868
- MAN: Oh, my God.
- Rawlings, look out!

137
00:12:25.993 --> 00:12:27.119
(MEN SHOUTING)

138
00:12:27.119 --> 00:12:30.164
RAWLINGS: Somebody help.
Get this... Get. Get.

139
00:12:31.123 --> 00:12:34.877
- Get.
- CASSID Y: Whiskey. Come on, get off him.

140
00:12:34.877 --> 00:12:36.420
(GROWLING)

141
00:12:36.420 --> 00:12:40.299
What's the matter there, cowboy?
Having a little trouble with the dogie?

142
00:12:41.842 --> 00:12:44.762
Whiskey is our squadron mascot.
Follow me.

143
00:12:45.721 --> 00:12:46.722
(STUTTERING)

144
00:12:46.847 --> 00:12:48.724
Who keeps a lion as a pet?

145
00:12:48.724 --> 00:12:51.852
Start over there.
I'll give you your room assignments.

146
00:12:53.729 --> 00:12:54.980
Jensen and Toddman.

147
00:12:55.064 --> 00:12:56.148
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

148
00:12:56.148 --> 00:12:57.066
Room one.

149
00:12:57.149 --> 00:12:59.777
Skinner and Lowry, room number three.

150
00:12:59.777 --> 00:13:03.113
- Excuse me. Skinner and I?
- Is there a problem?

151
00:13:07.493 --> 00:13:12.289
It would be like sharing a room
with one of my servants back home.

152
00:13:14.583 --> 00:13:17.711
Lowry, we'll put you in two with Beagle.

153
00:13:18.128 --> 00:13:21.673
Rawlings, you'll go in three with Skinner.

154
00:13:22.299 --> 00:13:26.595
If there are any further objections,
please take them up with Whiskey.

155
00:13:26.595 --> 00:13:27.596
Okay.

156
00:13:27.596 --> 00:13:29.806
I'll see you all at training
tomorrow morning at 6:30.

157
00:13:29.806 --> 00:13:31.350
JENSEN: Excuse me, sir?

158
00:13:31.475 --> 00:13:34.269
- Who rooms with the lion tamer?
- Cassidy?

159
00:13:34.269 --> 00:13:35.771
He has 20 kills.

160
00:13:35.771 --> 00:13:36.772
Twenty...

161
00:13:37.314 --> 00:13:39.399
He gets a room on his own.

162
00:13:46.698 --> 00:13:48.450
Let's get it over with.

163
00:13:48.700 --> 00:13:51.912
You got any objection to rooming
with a colored man?

164
00:13:51.787 --> 00:13:54.831
I don't know, you're the first one
I ever seen up close.

165
00:13:54.831 --> 00:13:56.708
What have you heard?

166
00:13:57.876 --> 00:14:00.670
I heard it's good luck to rub your head.

167
00:14:00.670 --> 00:14:04.007
- I wouldn't do that if I were you.
- Just telling you what I heard.

168
00:14:03.882 --> 00:14:05.800
Rub my head.

169
00:14:08.595 --> 00:14:12.349
- MAN: Think the drinks are free for flyboys?
- Maybe if it's water.

170
00:14:12.223 --> 00:14:13.475
(ALL LAUGHING)

171
00:14:14.434 --> 00:14:16.645
(MEN SINGING TAKE ME BACK
TO DEAR OLD BLIGHTY)

172
00:14:21.733 --> 00:14:23.401
(MEN CHATTERING)

173
00:14:37.999 --> 00:14:39.876
(MEN CHEERING)

174
00:14:44.339 --> 00:14:46.424
Sorry, gentlemen.

175
00:14:46.424 --> 00:14:50.720
I'm afraid I can't allow you entrance
into this fine establishment.

176
00:14:50.720 --> 00:14:53.765
This respite is reserved for killers.

177
00:14:56.559 --> 00:15:00.021
- You don't look like a killer to me.
- Don't I?

178
00:15:00.313 --> 00:15:02.690
I thought we all are on the same side.

179
00:15:02.690 --> 00:15:06.569
You shot down any Germans
I don't know about, chocolate?

180
00:15:08.529 --> 00:15:11.574
- Not yet.
- Then move on, chaps.

181
00:15:16.454 --> 00:15:18.372
Attaboy, fuzzy.

182
00:15:27.840 --> 00:15:30.051
Did you slip there, killer?

183
00:15:31.469 --> 00:15:32.636
CASSID Y: Sit down, Grant.

184
00:15:32.636 --> 00:15:35.139
- I can take him.
- No, you can't.

185
00:15:35.139 --> 00:15:36.182
He's a professional.

186
00:15:36.307 --> 00:15:39.518
I saw him fight in Paris.
He knocked a guy out in the eighth round.

187
00:15:39.393 --> 00:15:40.770
Sixth.

188
00:15:53.157 --> 00:15:55.075
(MEN SINGING)

189
00:15:55.242 --> 00:15:58.162
Now, as for all of us being
on the same side,

190
00:15:58.287 --> 00:16:01.081
until you actually do something,
you're not even in this war,

191
00:16:00.998 --> 00:16:02.583
let alone in this room.

192
00:16:02.666 --> 00:16:03.709
TODDMAN: Why not?

193
00:16:03.709 --> 00:16:07.046
We're all fighting for the French,
same as you.

194
00:16:08.088 --> 00:16:09.965
Not the same as me.

195
00:16:15.179 --> 00:16:17.264
Let's go, champ.

196
00:16:17.890 --> 00:16:19.683
(MEN CHEERING)

197
00:16:24.563 --> 00:16:26.648
SKINNER: Still wanna rub my head?

198
00:16:26.648 --> 00:16:27.691
(RAWLINGS LAUGHS)

199
00:16:32.613 --> 00:16:35.824
Gentlemen, this is the Nieuport 17.

200
00:16:35.824 --> 00:16:38.952
This plane is the newest French fighter.

201
00:16:39.369 --> 00:16:42.706
When you are proficient enough,
you'll be among the first to fly it.

202
00:16:42.623 --> 00:16:46.543
But remember, it is the man
and not the machine that matters.

203
00:16:46.668 --> 00:16:49.796
His bullet is no faster than yours.

204
00:16:49.713 --> 00:16:53.133
Go on your left. On your right.
Watch your back.

205
00:16:53.133 --> 00:16:54.718
Okay, Skinner.

206
00:16:55.635 --> 00:16:56.803
- That's good.
- I got that.

207
00:16:56.887 --> 00:16:58.221
Watch the fuel.

208
00:16:58.221 --> 00:17:01.892
If you run out of gas,
you will sleep with the Germans.

209
00:17:01.892 --> 00:17:04.186
(COUNTING IN FRENCH)

210
00:17:04.394 --> 00:17:05.437
Stop!

211
00:17:05.437 --> 00:17:07.647
Come on, Toddman. Watch your balance.

212
00:17:07.731 --> 00:17:11.151
No. Come on. Go, go, go.

213
00:17:11.151 --> 00:17:13.153
(COUNTING IN FRENCH)

214
00:17:13.236 --> 00:17:15.739
Come on, Jensen. Go, go, go, Jensen.

215
00:17:15.989 --> 00:17:19.075
Come on, Rawlings. Go, go. Come on.

216
00:17:18.992 --> 00:17:20.869
Watch your balance, no.

217
00:17:21.911 --> 00:17:23.079
Poor Skinner.

218
00:17:23.163 --> 00:17:25.248
A word about equipment.

219
00:17:25.749 --> 00:17:28.084
This is the Escadrille scarf.

220
00:17:29.335 --> 00:17:33.256
It is not just to make you
look good for the girls...

221
00:17:33.673 --> 00:17:34.924
What would he know about that?

222
00:17:34.924 --> 00:17:37.552
...but to keep your neck
from being irritated

223
00:17:37.552 --> 00:17:42.765
from the constant turning
to spot enemy aircraft.

224
00:17:43.099 --> 00:17:44.434
Contact.

225
00:17:49.355 --> 00:17:50.982
- Go on, Rawlings!
- Go, Rawlings!

226
00:17:50.982 --> 00:17:52.025
Go, Rawlings!

227
00:18:00.491 --> 00:18:02.035
- What?
- See it?

228
00:18:05.204 --> 00:18:07.040
(RAWLINGS WHOOPING)

229
00:18:11.127 --> 00:18:12.462
(ALL CHEERING)

230
00:18:13.921 --> 00:18:15.214
All right!

231
00:18:15.214 --> 00:18:16.966
You're on your own, yeah!

232
00:18:17.049 --> 00:18:18.426
He's going.

233
00:18:22.722 --> 00:18:25.224
- Go, Skinner.
- Skinner, let her rip.

234
00:18:25.641 --> 00:18:27.310
- All right, Beagle.
- Go get them. Get up there.

235
00:18:27.393 --> 00:18:28.853
Keep it straight.

236
00:18:29.979 --> 00:18:31.480
Come on, Lowry.

237
00:18:33.024 --> 00:18:38.779
GIROUX: Now that you are actually flying,
it is time to learn about tactics.

238
00:18:38.863 --> 00:18:41.574
Left. Right.

239
00:18:42.742 --> 00:18:43.743
- Both.
- Both.

240
00:18:44.910 --> 00:18:45.828
Right. Left.

241
00:18:46.078 --> 00:18:50.249
THENAULT: In any form of attack,
it is best to fire in short bursts.

242
00:18:50.124 --> 00:18:53.252
(IMITATING SHORT BURSTS
OF GUNFIRE)

243
00:18:56.380 --> 00:18:57.423
Follow him.

244
00:18:58.883 --> 00:18:59.925
(GUN FIRING)

245
00:18:59.925 --> 00:19:03.596
SKINNER: Give me right, give me right.
Good, give me left, give me left.

246
00:19:05.889 --> 00:19:06.932
- More your left.
- Left.

247
00:19:06.932 --> 00:19:10.561
Your primary goal is to get on their tail.

248
00:19:10.769 --> 00:19:13.355
This is your best shooting position.

249
00:19:16.692 --> 00:19:19.445
Beagle. The target, Beagle.

250
00:19:20.487 --> 00:19:23.365
Come on, Beagle. The target, Beagle!

251
00:19:23.490 --> 00:19:26.118
Go. Go, Rawlings. That's good.

252
00:19:26.535 --> 00:19:28.912
That's good. Go, Jensen.

253
00:19:28.912 --> 00:19:33.625
Go, Jensen. Good. Good, Skinner.
Good. Well done.

254
00:19:33.500 --> 00:19:36.962
THENAULT: We don't want you bringing
bullets home. We have millions.

255
00:19:36.962 --> 00:19:39.256
Leave the bullets up there.

256
00:19:39.882 --> 00:19:42.259
Let the Germans take them home.

257
00:19:43.302 --> 00:19:44.886
(GUNS FIRING)

258
00:19:54.479 --> 00:19:55.605
(MEN CHEERING)

259
00:19:55.731 --> 00:19:57.482
MAN: Good shot, Rawlings.

260
00:19:57.899 --> 00:19:58.817
Not bad.

261
00:19:59.067 --> 00:19:59.985
(SPEAKS FRENCH)

262
00:20:00.193 --> 00:20:02.988
TODDMAN: Good shooting, cowboy.
JENSEN: Way to go, Rawlings.

263
00:20:09.995 --> 00:20:11.329
GIROUX: Rawlings.

264
00:20:12.164 --> 00:20:15.000
I want you to go up with Beagle
and teach him how to shoot.

265
00:20:14.875 --> 00:20:17.168
Why me? You're the instructor.

266
00:20:17.294 --> 00:20:20.213
Because I'm tired of trying to teach him.

267
00:20:22.424 --> 00:20:23.758
All right.

268
00:20:29.472 --> 00:20:33.560
Beagle, you need to use
more right rudder when you dive.

269
00:20:33.560 --> 00:20:35.353
I know, I know.

270
00:20:36.062 --> 00:20:37.731
Get off my back.

271
00:20:40.358 --> 00:20:42.610
Notify this Hun's next of kin.

272
00:20:43.361 --> 00:20:45.029
(GUN FIRING)

273
00:20:45.780 --> 00:20:47.323
Right rudder!

274
00:20:49.534 --> 00:20:51.619
There's something wrong with the gun!

275
00:20:51.619 --> 00:20:53.997
I know I can fly and I know I can shoot!

276
00:20:54.205 --> 00:20:57.458
Yeah, you just can't do them
at the same time.

277
00:21:03.881 --> 00:21:06.718
- Where are we going?
- I don't know.

278
00:21:06.718 --> 00:21:09.971
BEAGLE: Let's just fly around a little.
Have some fun.

279
00:21:14.434 --> 00:21:16.519
It's a beautiful country.

280
00:21:16.936 --> 00:21:19.355
Can see why the French fight for it.

281
00:21:19.355 --> 00:21:21.941
- Hey, Rawlings.
- What?

282
00:21:22.567 --> 00:21:24.443
(ENGINE SPUTTERING)

283
00:21:25.903 --> 00:21:28.823
- We're out of gas.
- What?

284
00:21:28.823 --> 00:21:32.368
- You didn't check it when we took off?
- I thought you did.

285
00:21:32.368 --> 00:21:34.453
You're the damn pilot!

286
00:21:34.745 --> 00:21:35.913
RAWLINGS: All right.

287
00:21:36.038 --> 00:21:39.667
Beagle, put it down over there. Over there.

288
00:21:39.667 --> 00:21:43.004
- No, there's more room over there.
- RAWLINGS: That terrain's too rough.

289
00:21:42.920 --> 00:21:45.006
- Put it over there.
- BEAGLE: What terrain?

290
00:21:45.089 --> 00:21:47.591
- RAWLINGS: Watch your airspeed.
- I got it.

291
00:21:47.591 --> 00:21:50.511
- We're going too fast!
- BEAGLE: Just shut up!

292
00:21:52.721 --> 00:21:54.181
(GROANING)

293
00:21:54.974 --> 00:21:56.767
(CRASHING)

294
00:22:01.147 --> 00:22:03.440
(WOMEN MURMURING IN FRENCH)

295
00:22:12.408 --> 00:22:14.702
(SPEAKING FRENCH)

296
00:22:15.327 --> 00:22:16.787
Where am I?

297
00:22:23.460 --> 00:22:26.880
Where's my... Where's my plane? My leg.

298
00:22:33.137 --> 00:22:36.890
Is this a... What do you call it?

299
00:22:39.393 --> 00:22:42.312
Do you speak English?

300
00:22:44.231 --> 00:22:47.734
- Hey, Rawlings, you came to.
- How'd we get here, ace?

301
00:22:47.734 --> 00:22:50.779
Well, first of all,
you left the plane in kind of a hurry.

302
00:22:50.779 --> 00:22:53.824
Then this one found you out back
and helped carry you in.

303
00:22:54.950 --> 00:22:56.326
This ain't so bad.

304
00:22:56.326 --> 00:22:58.495
(CLARISE SPEAKING FRENCH)

305
00:23:03.583 --> 00:23:05.502
(ALL CHATTERING)

306
00:23:12.342 --> 00:23:14.136
(SPEAKING FRENCH)

307
00:23:19.349 --> 00:23:21.851
You want me to take my pants off?

308
00:23:23.436 --> 00:23:24.771
Okay.

309
00:23:39.869 --> 00:23:41.871
You seem to be in good hands here.

310
00:23:41.871 --> 00:23:44.707
I'm gonna go see if anybody wants
to look after my leg.

311
00:23:44.791 --> 00:23:46.251
Oh, girls?

312
00:23:52.799 --> 00:23:57.512
So you're a prostitute?

313
00:23:59.180 --> 00:24:01.683
I mean, you don't look like one.

314
00:24:03.559 --> 00:24:05.436
You're very pretty.

315
00:24:05.728 --> 00:24:07.522
You understand? Pretty?

316
00:24:08.231 --> 00:24:10.024
Pretty...

317
00:24:12.735 --> 00:24:13.653
Like...

318
00:24:15.154 --> 00:24:16.155
Like the...

319
00:24:17.532 --> 00:24:20.993
The flower is pretty.

320
00:24:21.911 --> 00:24:25.248
And you are pretty like a flower.

321
00:24:25.164 --> 00:24:27.416
And you are pretty like a flower.

322
00:24:29.627 --> 00:24:31.170
Hey, Rawlings.

323
00:24:31.295 --> 00:24:33.506
You know, they don't give medals
for running out of gas.

324
00:24:33.589 --> 00:24:36.509
- You here to take us back?
- Yeah, but what's the hurry?

325
00:24:36.425 --> 00:24:37.426
Hey, watch it.

326
00:24:37.552 --> 00:24:39.929
What the hell?
She's a chippie, not a nurse.

327
00:24:40.680 --> 00:24:44.767
You do realize that crash landing
your own plane doesn't count as combat.

328
00:24:44.850 --> 00:24:46.727
Sorry about that.

329
00:24:47.269 --> 00:24:51.440
Listen, it was...
It was really nice to meet you.

330
00:24:53.109 --> 00:24:54.360
Yeah.

331
00:24:55.694 --> 00:24:57.780
That was... That was for you.

332
00:25:01.117 --> 00:25:02.159
(CHICKEN CLUCKING)

333
00:25:02.993 --> 00:25:04.870
(SPEAKING FRENCH)

334
00:25:07.790 --> 00:25:09.792
(WOMEN SPEAKING FRENCH)

335
00:25:13.295 --> 00:25:15.714
That guy knows how to live.

336
00:25:16.215 --> 00:25:17.883
(ALL CHATTERING)

337
00:25:19.551 --> 00:25:22.304
Guess all his friends aren't dead.

338
00:25:24.139 --> 00:25:27.309
Come on, Rawlings,
we've got a long drive home.

339
00:25:29.895 --> 00:25:32.606
TODDMAN: Hey, Rawlings.
Meet the new arrivals.

340
00:25:32.606 --> 00:25:34.274
I was just showing them around.

341
00:25:34.400 --> 00:25:37.736
Those circular tents at the back
are where the crew live.

342
00:25:37.611 --> 00:25:39.696
And you guys already know
where the canteen is.

343
00:25:39.696 --> 00:25:41.782
Nunn will be sneaking in there
looking for cookies.

344
00:25:41.907 --> 00:25:43.742
He's got a sweet tooth. Right, Nunn?

345
00:25:43.742 --> 00:25:47.329
- Nunn doesn't say a whole lot.
- I can, if something comes up.

346
00:25:47.204 --> 00:25:49.581
TODDMAN: That's the mess hall
and the officers' club.

347
00:25:49.581 --> 00:25:51.083
No chapel?

348
00:25:51.166 --> 00:25:53.585
Fellows, meet Porter.

349
00:25:54.002 --> 00:25:57.923
- You religious?
- I keep my Bible close.

350
00:25:57.839 --> 00:26:00.550
What's a man of God doing here at war?

351
00:26:00.968 --> 00:26:03.595
Hopefully the same thing you are.

352
00:26:04.096 --> 00:26:07.015
DEWITT: How are the barracks, by the way?
TODDMAN: Yeah.

353
00:26:07.849 --> 00:26:11.269
- Nothing fancy.
- BEAGLE: Yeah, nothing fancy.

354
00:26:29.454 --> 00:26:31.122
(GROANS)

355
00:26:54.479 --> 00:26:56.564
(ENGINES WHIRRING)

356
00:27:46.781 --> 00:27:49.951
- Whose planes are these?
- They are yours.

357
00:28:03.172 --> 00:28:04.215
Hey!

358
00:28:04.965 --> 00:28:06.300
- Are those really ours?
- These really are amazing.

359
00:28:06.300 --> 00:28:07.885
- We get to fly them?
- These are great.

360
00:28:07.968 --> 00:28:09.970
Merry Christmas, boys.

361
00:28:10.054 --> 00:28:12.890
- This one's mine.
- Almost makes you feel sorry for the Huns.

362
00:28:12.890 --> 00:28:14.308
My, oh, my.

363
00:28:14.433 --> 00:28:17.228
So why do they all have
Indian heads on them?

364
00:28:17.228 --> 00:28:19.230
It is the Escadrille insignia.

365
00:28:19.230 --> 00:28:21.732
Well, why that?
I mean, Indians were defeated.

366
00:28:21.732 --> 00:28:25.069
Yeah, but they were brave. I like it.

367
00:28:25.069 --> 00:28:29.865
You're allowed to have a personal insignia
on the forward part of the fuselage.

368
00:28:29.740 --> 00:28:32.493
Well, that's good.
Let them know who we are.

369
00:28:32.493 --> 00:28:36.330
I've already picked this one out
for myself, so hands off.

370
00:28:37.247 --> 00:28:39.583
No, Skinner, find your own.

371
00:29:00.437 --> 00:29:03.231
It's great. Looks just like it.

372
00:29:04.274 --> 00:29:07.194
- Hey, Lowry, that's good.
- Thanks, Jensen.

373
00:29:07.194 --> 00:29:11.573
I was going to be an artist,
until my father thought better of it.

374
00:29:11.865 --> 00:29:13.533
Would you paint me a knight?

375
00:29:13.533 --> 00:29:15.535
We're kind of like flying knights,
don't you think?

376
00:29:15.535 --> 00:29:17.287
- Sure.
- Thanks.

377
00:29:17.412 --> 00:29:19.372
(MEN CHATTERING IN FRENCH)

378
00:29:21.792 --> 00:29:24.503
- RAWLINGS: What's that, Nunn?
- A woodpecker.

379
00:29:24.628 --> 00:29:26.463
That ought to really scare them.

380
00:29:26.588 --> 00:29:28.965
I think it says we're gonna put
a whole bunch of holes in them.

381
00:29:28.965 --> 00:29:32.135
I think that it says that you've got
a bunch of holes in your brain.

382
00:29:32.010 --> 00:29:34.221
Whatever it is, get it done.

383
00:29:34.221 --> 00:29:36.181
We're going to war in two days.

384
00:29:36.306 --> 00:29:38.141
Knights of the air.

385
00:29:41.728 --> 00:29:44.314
What? We are. We're like knights.

386
00:29:44.314 --> 00:29:47.317
The Germans are moving
toward the Meuse River

387
00:29:47.317 --> 00:29:50.070
as part of their push to take Paris.

388
00:29:50.570 --> 00:29:53.698
In order to stop their advance
in our sector,

389
00:29:53.698 --> 00:29:57.660
you will rendezvous over Doulcon
with two Handley Page bombers

390
00:29:57.660 --> 00:30:01.498
at 0600 tomorrow
and escort them to Jametz

391
00:30:01.414 --> 00:30:05.793
where they are to destroy the main
German ammunition and supply depot.

392
00:30:06.503 --> 00:30:10.673
It is heavily fortified
by observation balloons,

393
00:30:10.673 --> 00:30:17.597
cables on three sides,
and Archie batteries in these six positions.

394
00:30:17.889 --> 00:30:20.808
Cassidy will be your squadron leader.

395
00:30:20.933 --> 00:30:23.102
He'll be watching over you.

396
00:30:23.853 --> 00:30:25.813
Remember your training.

397
00:30:25.813 --> 00:30:28.608
Don't fly straight lines.

398
00:30:28.733 --> 00:30:32.612
Be an elusive target
and an efficient hunter.

399
00:30:34.280 --> 00:30:35.823
Any questions?

400
00:30:36.866 --> 00:30:38.201
Yes, sir.

401
00:30:38.743 --> 00:30:40.828
Will we be back by lunch?

402
00:30:40.828 --> 00:30:42.371
(MEN SNICKERING)

403
00:30:44.457 --> 00:30:47.084
I meant any intelligent questions.

404
00:30:47.793 --> 00:30:51.964
I'm sorry, just trying to loosen things up.

405
00:30:52.214 --> 00:30:53.341
Don't.

406
00:31:10.566 --> 00:31:11.984
BEAGLE: Hey, fellows.

407
00:31:12.318 --> 00:31:15.237
What do you think I ought
to wear tomorrow? Yellow or purple?

408
00:31:15.237 --> 00:31:17.531
Anything but the pink.
You get shot down in that,

409
00:31:17.531 --> 00:31:20.576
you're gonna embarrass
the entire Escadrille.

410
00:31:24.496 --> 00:31:27.666
What are you talking
about getting shot down for?

411
00:31:27.666 --> 00:31:29.835
What's the matter, you nervous?

412
00:31:30.878 --> 00:31:34.214
Hell, no. You? You brought it up.

413
00:31:34.840 --> 00:31:38.927
We're all nervous, except Porter.

414
00:31:39.011 --> 00:31:41.013
He's got religion on his side.

415
00:31:42.681 --> 00:31:44.433
I'm not nervous.

416
00:31:44.850 --> 00:31:48.520
Hey, it's all right to be a little edgy
before a fight.

417
00:31:48.395 --> 00:31:51.732
Keeps you sharp. Isn't that right, Skinner?

418
00:31:52.566 --> 00:31:56.528
The fights I been in,
they don't shoot at you.

419
00:31:59.239 --> 00:32:01.867
We should hit the sack. We get up at 4:00.

420
00:32:06.538 --> 00:32:07.873
Rawlings.

421
00:32:07.873 --> 00:32:08.957
(GROWLING)

422
00:32:11.877 --> 00:32:14.046
I wanna see you for a minute.

423
00:32:20.093 --> 00:32:21.344
(ROARS)

424
00:32:26.641 --> 00:32:28.310
Just saying hello.

425
00:32:29.978 --> 00:32:31.146
Hello.

426
00:32:31.354 --> 00:32:32.731
(GRUNTING)

427
00:32:33.148 --> 00:32:34.816
Come on in.

428
00:32:37.319 --> 00:32:39.404
I was looking at your file,

429
00:32:39.571 --> 00:32:42.073
and it's my job to write a letter home
to your parents

430
00:32:42.073 --> 00:32:44.075
if anything should happen to you.

431
00:32:44.075 --> 00:32:48.663
Since both your parents are dead,
who's your next of kin?

432
00:32:48.997 --> 00:32:52.208
I don't know. I don't really have any.

433
00:32:59.007 --> 00:33:00.258
(SIGHING)

434
00:33:00.425 --> 00:33:06.181
You know, if you die here,
your family name dies with you.

435
00:33:06.514 --> 00:33:09.100
Well, I don't plan on dying.

436
00:33:09.100 --> 00:33:12.520
None of the guys
in the squadron cemetery did either.

437
00:33:14.731 --> 00:33:16.190
Think about it.

438
00:33:18.192 --> 00:33:19.527
(GROWLING)

439
00:33:22.864 --> 00:33:25.450
Yeah, I'll think about that, sir.

440
00:33:34.042 --> 00:33:35.585
(GROWLING)

441
00:33:36.419 --> 00:33:37.670
Stay.

442
00:34:04.071 --> 00:34:05.823
(SPEAKING LATIN)

443
00:34:07.074 --> 00:34:08.659
- GIROUX: Lowry?
- Yes, sir.

444
00:34:08.659 --> 00:34:11.037
If you feel you're gonna crash,
take off your goggles

445
00:34:11.037 --> 00:34:13.330
because the glass can cut
your eyes, d'accord?

446
00:34:18.335 --> 00:34:21.464
- Hey, you're still here, Rawlings.
- Yeah.

447
00:34:22.006 --> 00:34:23.841
Thought I'd take my chances.

448
00:34:25.217 --> 00:34:26.677
What's this?

449
00:34:27.595 --> 00:34:30.764
It's just the brand of the ranch
my family owned

450
00:34:31.181 --> 00:34:33.350
till the bank foreclosed.

451
00:34:34.935 --> 00:34:36.895
Beagle, get here.

452
00:34:39.607 --> 00:34:43.861
If your guns jam, it sometimes helps
to bang on the cocking handle.

453
00:34:46.196 --> 00:34:47.322
What's this for?

454
00:34:47.322 --> 00:34:50.451
Plane catches fire, you got three choices.

455
00:34:50.451 --> 00:34:53.287
Can stay in it and burn
with it all the way to the ground,

456
00:34:53.287 --> 00:34:55.789
you can jump from several thousand feet,

457
00:34:56.081 --> 00:34:59.418
or you can take the quick
and painless way out.

458
00:35:00.127 --> 00:35:01.712
Good luck, gentlemen.

459
00:35:05.048 --> 00:35:06.800
- MAN: Contact!
- Contact.

460
00:36:08.778 --> 00:36:11.030
(COUNTING IN FRENCH)

461
00:36:41.185 --> 00:36:43.146
(SPEAKING FRENCH)

462
00:36:57.869 --> 00:36:59.120
(SHOUTING IN GERMAN)

463
00:37:20.808 --> 00:37:22.184
I'm going up.

464
00:38:40.053 --> 00:38:41.429
JENSEN: Toddman!

465
00:38:54.651 --> 00:38:56.403
(GUNS FIRING)

466
00:39:23.847 --> 00:39:26.266
(METALLIC RATTLING)

467
00:40:04.428 --> 00:40:06.514
(WHOOPING) Yeah!

468
00:40:30.996 --> 00:40:37.670
Rawlings! I made it!
I'm all right! Go get them!

469
00:40:57.356 --> 00:40:59.149
(GUNS FIRING)

470
00:41:48.073 --> 00:41:50.242
(COUNTING IN FRENCH)

471
00:41:57.457 --> 00:41:59.417
(GIROUX COUNTING IN FRENCH)

472
00:42:01.294 --> 00:42:02.963
(MEN SHOUTING)

473
00:42:22.232 --> 00:42:24.025
Bastards were everywhere, sir.

474
00:42:24.025 --> 00:42:26.319
CASSID Y: We got jumped
before we reached Jametz.

475
00:42:26.319 --> 00:42:28.488
They were all over us.
We never even made it to the bombers.

476
00:42:28.488 --> 00:42:30.281
- Where is Dewitt?
- Didn't make it.

477
00:42:30.406 --> 00:42:31.533
- And Toddman?
- CASSID Y: Nope.

478
00:42:31.533 --> 00:42:34.577
Toddman was right there.
He was right there. Then he was gone.

479
00:42:34.577 --> 00:42:37.163
- Anybody see what happened to Nunn?
- Sir.

480
00:42:37.163 --> 00:42:40.416
He had to put it down.
He made it safely to the ground

481
00:42:40.416 --> 00:42:43.503
and this German dived on him and
shot him right when he was sitting there.

482
00:42:43.503 --> 00:42:46.464
- He had a black falcon on his plane?
- Yeah.

483
00:42:47.590 --> 00:42:48.633
Something should be done.

484
00:42:48.633 --> 00:42:50.843
I mean, you don't just shoot
an airman on the ground.

485
00:42:50.843 --> 00:42:53.846
- Mission debriefing in 15 minutes.
- What about Nunn?

486
00:42:53.846 --> 00:42:55.181
He was just sitting there on the ground!

487
00:42:55.181 --> 00:42:58.101
A lot has happened in this war
before you got to it.

488
00:42:58.101 --> 00:43:01.270
I thought there was supposed to be
some sort of honor in the way we fight.

489
00:43:01.270 --> 00:43:04.690
Reports can be filed. But you want justice?

490
00:43:04.690 --> 00:43:08.361
You're the man in the air,
you're the man with the gun.

491
00:43:16.285 --> 00:43:17.536
Contact.

492
00:43:17.536 --> 00:43:19.372
(ENGINE STARTING)

493
00:43:19.372 --> 00:43:21.916
Get those streamers off my plane.

494
00:43:25.419 --> 00:43:27.004
(GROWLING)

495
00:43:33.052 --> 00:43:35.846
- What's he doing?
- He's going back up.

496
00:43:36.305 --> 00:43:38.974
- After what?
- Whatever he can find.

497
00:43:40.559 --> 00:43:43.062
- He's going alone?
- Yeah.

498
00:43:43.896 --> 00:43:45.773
He prefers it that way.

499
00:43:51.737 --> 00:43:54.823
I had no idea
that it was going to be like that.

500
00:43:55.282 --> 00:43:57.368
Do better next time.

501
00:43:58.077 --> 00:43:59.828
Soon as I get one kill,

502
00:43:59.828 --> 00:44:01.830
show my father
that I was in the thick of it,

503
00:44:01.830 --> 00:44:03.916
that's it, I'm going home.

504
00:44:08.295 --> 00:44:11.507
RAWLINGS: Went right through there.
Almost lost this.

505
00:44:14.676 --> 00:44:17.179
- You get any?
- Not the one I wanted.

506
00:44:17.471 --> 00:44:19.264
Not the Black Falcon.

507
00:44:21.934 --> 00:44:22.601
GRANT: Oi.

508
00:44:24.353 --> 00:44:26.647
Where the hell do you think you're off to?

509
00:44:26.647 --> 00:44:28.315
Not tonight, Grant.

510
00:44:30.275 --> 00:44:32.361
You're not going anywhere.

511
00:44:33.862 --> 00:44:35.947
Not till you drink with us.

512
00:44:36.031 --> 00:44:39.368
- I thought it was only for killers.
- You'll do.

513
00:44:43.955 --> 00:44:45.540
(MEN SINGING)

514
00:44:48.752 --> 00:44:53.548
Drink up, Rawlings.
You're still alive. That's something.

515
00:44:55.217 --> 00:44:56.676
I don't feel like it.

516
00:44:56.801 --> 00:44:59.471
The first time is always your hardest.

517
00:44:59.596 --> 00:45:01.556
To losing your virginity!

518
00:45:01.681 --> 00:45:03.350
(ALL CHEERING)

519
00:45:08.480 --> 00:45:11.900
Does anyone here care
that three pilots died today?

520
00:45:12.108 --> 00:45:13.485
Pilots die every day.

521
00:45:13.568 --> 00:45:15.028
Have a drink. Calm down.

522
00:45:15.028 --> 00:45:17.739
I don't wanna calm down.
I wanna honor the men who died.

523
00:45:17.739 --> 00:45:20.575
Yeah, well, this is how we honor them.

524
00:45:20.867 --> 00:45:23.369
It's how we've always honored them.

525
00:45:23.578 --> 00:45:25.455
Now, none of us knows
how much time we have left,

526
00:45:25.455 --> 00:45:30.168
so we can't waste it sitting around
grieving about things we can't change.

527
00:45:31.419 --> 00:45:34.005
So you can either join in

528
00:45:34.923 --> 00:45:38.593
or you can go up to your room
and cry like a little baby.

529
00:45:38.593 --> 00:45:40.261
You suit yourself.

530
00:45:40.678 --> 00:45:42.138
(MAN CHEERS)

531
00:45:42.138 --> 00:45:43.932
(MEN SINGING)

532
00:45:57.862 --> 00:46:00.073
GRANT: Wake up, Rawlings. We're here.

533
00:46:01.741 --> 00:46:03.284
(MUSIC PLAYING ON RADIO)

534
00:46:03.284 --> 00:46:04.452
Hello.

535
00:46:04.535 --> 00:46:06.120
(GREETS IN FRENCH)

536
00:46:06.120 --> 00:46:08.206
I'm looking for the owner.

537
00:46:08.414 --> 00:46:10.708
No English. No English.

538
00:46:12.585 --> 00:46:15.713
- The owner of the house?
- I am the owner.

539
00:46:16.339 --> 00:46:21.052
Hi. I'm Blaine Rawlings.
I'm looking for a girl.

540
00:46:21.052 --> 00:46:22.303
You might remember me.

541
00:46:22.386 --> 00:46:26.349
- I injured my leg and she bandaged it up.
- Oh, Lucienne.

542
00:46:27.600 --> 00:46:30.519
Maybe. She was wearing a brown skirt.

543
00:46:30.728 --> 00:46:33.314
But Lucienne is not one of my girls.

544
00:46:33.647 --> 00:46:35.733
- She's not?
- No, she does not work here.

545
00:46:35.733 --> 00:46:39.820
She was exchanging supplies,
a round of Brie for some chocolate.

546
00:46:44.074 --> 00:46:46.494
A round of Brie for some chocolate.

547
00:46:46.660 --> 00:46:47.912
Madam?

548
00:46:48.746 --> 00:46:49.914
Madam.

549
00:46:50.247 --> 00:46:52.499
That girl, Lucienne,

550
00:46:53.584 --> 00:46:55.336
do you know where she lives?

551
00:46:55.336 --> 00:46:58.172
Down the Marlier Road,
about five kilometers.

552
00:46:58.672 --> 00:46:59.715
A small château,

553
00:46:59.715 --> 00:47:03.594
And how about that horse outside?
Do you know who owns that?

554
00:47:09.600 --> 00:47:11.268
(SQUAWKING)

555
00:47:36.710 --> 00:47:38.712
(SPEAKING FRENCH)

556
00:47:48.305 --> 00:47:49.347
(RESPONDS IN FRENCH)

557
00:47:51.641 --> 00:47:52.684
Right.

558
00:48:04.237 --> 00:48:05.739
(GREETS IN FRENCH)

559
00:48:11.995 --> 00:48:13.538
(SPEAKING FRENCH)

560
00:48:14.247 --> 00:48:15.332
What?

561
00:48:22.172 --> 00:48:23.256
You know,

562
00:48:24.799 --> 00:48:28.762
- I'm mad at you. I'm mad. Understand?
- No.

563
00:48:29.596 --> 00:48:32.015
I'm mad. I'm mad at you.

564
00:48:32.015 --> 00:48:33.683
(ROARS MOCKINGLY)

565
00:48:34.809 --> 00:48:38.354
Because you made me think
that you were a prostitute.

566
00:48:39.272 --> 00:48:40.773
- You know?
- No.

567
00:48:44.194 --> 00:48:45.528
One moment.

568
00:48:49.949 --> 00:48:51.784
(QUESTIONS IN FRENCH)

569
00:48:55.121 --> 00:48:56.080
You?

570
00:48:57.123 --> 00:48:58.374
Are you?

571
00:48:59.542 --> 00:49:00.543
No.

572
00:49:01.627 --> 00:49:02.545
Well.

573
00:49:03.588 --> 00:49:04.630
(SPEAKS FRENCH)

574
00:49:04.714 --> 00:49:05.882
Am I?

575
00:49:06.924 --> 00:49:07.884
No.

576
00:49:09.844 --> 00:49:10.887
No.

577
00:49:12.763 --> 00:49:16.934
No, I came because I wanted to see you.

578
00:49:16.809 --> 00:49:17.977
(SPEAKING FRENCH)

579
00:49:18.060 --> 00:49:20.897
I wanted to see

580
00:49:23.065 --> 00:49:24.025
you.

581
00:49:30.281 --> 00:49:33.743
Why did you pretend to...

582
00:49:37.371 --> 00:49:38.914
(CLEARS THROAT)

583
00:49:39.999 --> 00:49:42.793
I afraid.

584
00:49:44.587 --> 00:49:46.130
You're afraid?

585
00:49:47.673 --> 00:49:48.757
Why?

586
00:49:49.049 --> 00:49:50.092
(SPEAKS FRENCH)

587
00:49:53.846 --> 00:49:54.889
You

588
00:49:57.266 --> 00:49:59.602
die soon.

589
00:50:08.027 --> 00:50:10.946
Are these your children?

590
00:50:10.946 --> 00:50:12.531
(SPEAKING FRENCH)

591
00:50:16.994 --> 00:50:18.787
- Oh, no.
- No?

592
00:50:21.874 --> 00:50:23.792
They're your brother's?

593
00:50:26.795 --> 00:50:28.046
- Wife.
- Wife.

594
00:50:28.046 --> 00:50:29.089
Wife?

595
00:50:29.214 --> 00:50:32.551
Your brother and his wife's?
Their children? Oh.

596
00:50:36.054 --> 00:50:37.139
Die?

597
00:50:38.974 --> 00:50:40.142
They died?

598
00:50:42.853 --> 00:50:43.812
Yes.

599
00:50:48.275 --> 00:50:49.318
(SPEAKING FRENCH)

600
00:50:56.199 --> 00:50:57.242
(IMITATES EXPLOSION)

601
00:51:02.330 --> 00:51:04.833
Brother et wife.

602
00:51:10.255 --> 00:51:11.631
I'm sorry.

603
00:51:13.425 --> 00:51:17.345
The enfants must be sad.

604
00:51:22.892 --> 00:51:24.352
I have an idea.

605
00:51:25.186 --> 00:51:26.229
Come on.

606
00:51:28.606 --> 00:51:30.942
(IMITATING GUN FIRING)

607
00:51:36.448 --> 00:51:38.116
(WHOOPING)

608
00:51:44.289 --> 00:51:45.832
(GROANING)

609
00:51:46.040 --> 00:51:47.208
(SNICKERING)

610
00:51:50.962 --> 00:51:51.963
Hey!

611
00:51:52.630 --> 00:51:55.550
Hey. Hey! Hey!

612
00:51:57.927 --> 00:52:00.430
(EX CLAIMING IN FRENCH)

613
00:52:00.430 --> 00:52:01.973
(ALL CHUCKLING)

614
00:52:02.932 --> 00:52:04.308
Thank you.

615
00:52:05.727 --> 00:52:07.311
Did you like it?

616
00:52:07.520 --> 00:52:09.897
Does that mean I can come back?

617
00:52:11.816 --> 00:52:13.901
Can I come see you again?

618
00:52:14.068 --> 00:52:15.987
(SPEAKING FRENCH)

619
00:52:15.987 --> 00:52:17.947
No, not the kids. You.

620
00:52:18.489 --> 00:52:20.992
Would you like to see me again?

621
00:52:23.578 --> 00:52:24.620
All right, bye.

622
00:52:27.957 --> 00:52:29.834
What are you gonna do?

623
00:52:31.168 --> 00:52:32.837
(SIREN BLARING)

624
00:52:33.921 --> 00:52:35.881
(CHATTERING)

625
00:52:36.716 --> 00:52:40.052
The Germans just bombed
the railway yard at Revigny.

626
00:52:40.177 --> 00:52:43.264
If you hurry, you can cut them off.

627
00:52:43.806 --> 00:52:46.726
It is a chance to be more aggressive
in your tactics.

628
00:52:46.726 --> 00:52:47.685
I want those chocks.

629
00:52:47.852 --> 00:52:51.439
If you do well,
you may get another chance at Jametz.

630
00:52:51.939 --> 00:52:55.067
Let's get the jump
and dictate the engagement.

631
00:52:55.276 --> 00:52:56.318
Hurry.

632
00:52:57.278 --> 00:52:59.446
Come on, let's go.

633
00:53:04.660 --> 00:53:06.537
(MAN SHOUTING)

634
00:53:06.537 --> 00:53:09.123
Come on, I'm keeping you guys alive.

635
00:53:16.130 --> 00:53:17.589
(GUNS FIRING)

636
00:54:07.514 --> 00:54:09.099
(GROANING)

637
00:54:33.498 --> 00:54:34.958
(GRUNTING)

638
00:54:40.713 --> 00:54:42.382
(GUNS FIRING)

639
00:54:56.563 --> 00:54:57.981
(SINGING HYMN)

640
00:56:20.980 --> 00:56:22.773
(GUNS FIRING)

641
00:56:43.919 --> 00:56:45.712
(HAMMER CLINKING)

642
00:57:13.532 --> 00:57:15.534
(GUN FIRING)

643
00:58:04.249 --> 00:58:06.084
SKINNER: Now that's more like it.

644
00:58:06.084 --> 00:58:08.086
We really stitched them up good today.

645
00:58:08.169 --> 00:58:09.337
What?

646
00:58:09.337 --> 00:58:12.048
It's so goddamn noisy up there.
I can't hear a thing.

647
00:58:12.173 --> 00:58:15.385
You got two today, Blaine.
You're our ace so far.

648
00:58:15.593 --> 00:58:18.096
Well, you fired enough to take down six.

649
00:58:18.513 --> 00:58:21.349
You ever think about trying to miss,
Beagle? You might do better.

650
00:58:21.349 --> 00:58:22.767
I told you, my gun's all screwy.

651
00:58:22.892 --> 00:58:24.852
Oh, really? It's your gun, is it?

652
00:58:24.852 --> 00:58:26.104
What are you trying to say, Lowry?

653
00:58:26.104 --> 00:58:27.688
Cut it out.

654
00:58:27.772 --> 00:58:30.191
Someone should mention Porter.
He got one.

655
00:58:30.191 --> 00:58:31.776
Yeah, well, I was lucky.

656
00:58:31.776 --> 00:58:33.736
Germans just didn't want
to hear you sing anymore.

657
00:58:33.736 --> 00:58:35.613
Hey. Where's Higgins?

658
00:58:37.615 --> 00:58:38.616
No.

659
00:58:39.784 --> 00:58:41.452
I gotta sit down.

660
00:58:45.414 --> 00:58:47.708
- Is it bad?
- You're all right.

661
00:58:48.542 --> 00:58:50.628
Bullet went right by you.

662
00:58:54.298 --> 00:58:56.258
(MEN CHATTERING)

663
00:58:57.635 --> 00:58:58.761
(ALL APPLAUDING)

664
00:58:58.886 --> 00:59:00.137
There's our men!

665
00:59:01.263 --> 00:59:03.474
The Yanks got their first Huns.

666
00:59:03.474 --> 00:59:05.559
- Good show.
- Well done. Excellent.

667
00:59:06.060 --> 00:59:08.646
Now you're officially killers.

668
00:59:09.313 --> 00:59:10.314
GRANT: Come here, lads.

669
00:59:10.314 --> 00:59:11.690
Well done.

670
00:59:18.989 --> 00:59:22.117
We call this the Bottle of Death.

671
00:59:23.994 --> 00:59:26.914
You get one swig
for every plane you down.

672
00:59:28.248 --> 00:59:32.753
Only reason I'm still alive is some German
let me go when my gun jammed.

673
00:59:32.669 --> 00:59:34.505
I don't know why the hell he did it.

674
00:59:34.505 --> 00:59:37.549
CASSID Y: Did he have
two crossed swords on his plane?

675
00:59:39.510 --> 00:59:42.763
Franz Wolfert. A triple ace.

676
00:59:45.891 --> 00:59:48.519
He did it
because of what happened to Nunn.

677
00:59:48.393 --> 00:59:50.479
He won't let you off again.

678
00:59:52.689 --> 00:59:55.192
We know what happened to Higgins.

679
00:59:56.318 --> 00:59:57.569
Drink up.

680
01:00:08.121 --> 01:00:09.956
(MEN CHEERING)

681
01:00:15.212 --> 01:00:17.047
- Porter.
- I don't drink.

682
01:00:17.047 --> 01:00:18.131
(ALL EX CLAIMING)

683
01:00:18.131 --> 01:00:19.257
- Come on.
- Take a drink...

684
01:00:19.382 --> 01:00:21.468
- I don't drink.
- Come on.

685
01:00:21.468 --> 01:00:22.385
- Take a drink.
- Drink up.

686
01:00:22.469 --> 01:00:26.556
- Drink, drink, drink, drink!
- Drink, drink, drink, drink!

687
01:00:26.556 --> 01:00:27.807
(ALL CHEERING)

688
01:00:27.807 --> 01:00:29.476
(COUGHING)

689
01:00:30.644 --> 01:00:32.187
(PIANO PLAYING)

690
01:00:32.395 --> 01:00:34.689
(MEN SINGING)

691
01:00:39.152 --> 01:00:41.154
PORTER: Those guys sure can
tie one on. I mean...

692
01:00:41.154 --> 01:00:42.197
BEAGLE: Yeah.

693
01:00:42.197 --> 01:00:43.990
...the more they fly, the more they drink.
- Yeah.

694
01:00:44.074 --> 01:00:46.785
Except for Cassidy.
He just goes on even more missions.

695
01:00:46.785 --> 01:00:48.995
The man's a mystery. He's not human.

696
01:00:48.995 --> 01:00:50.663
We don't even know where he's from.

697
01:00:50.663 --> 01:00:54.084
I heard that he lost his family
in an electrical fire.

698
01:00:54.084 --> 01:00:56.795
- Did you hear that?
- I heard he flew for Pancho Villa.

699
01:00:56.795 --> 01:00:57.837
So he's a mercenary?

700
01:00:57.837 --> 01:00:59.422
Why don't somebody just ask?

701
01:00:59.422 --> 01:01:02.634
Well, he's not too chatty
about his personal life.

702
01:01:02.634 --> 01:01:04.302
I'd just be happy he's flying on our side.

703
01:01:04.427 --> 01:01:05.345
Yeah.

704
01:01:05.553 --> 01:01:07.847
Especially with the new tri-wings
the Germans got,

705
01:01:07.847 --> 01:01:09.849
125-horsepower engines.

706
01:01:09.849 --> 01:01:13.269
Nine-millimeter Spandau machine guns
with twice the ammo capacity.

707
01:01:13.269 --> 01:01:16.272
They can out-turn us
and they have a 1,000 feet-a-minute climb.

708
01:01:16.272 --> 01:01:17.940
They're the most maneuverable planes
in the sky.

709
01:01:17.940 --> 01:01:20.026
Well, yeah, maybe you'd be happier
fighting for them.

710
01:01:20.026 --> 01:01:22.445
Yeah. A lot fewer of our guys
would get shot.

711
01:01:22.445 --> 01:01:23.780
Real funny.

712
01:01:25.281 --> 01:01:27.033
- Hey, listen.
- What?

713
01:01:27.950 --> 01:01:30.578
There's something not right about Beagle,
you know?

714
01:01:30.578 --> 01:01:31.621
What do you mean?

715
01:01:31.621 --> 01:01:35.041
- I mean, he doesn't get any mail, right?
- So?

716
01:01:35.041 --> 01:01:37.793
Yeah, he never hits
any of the Germans he shoots at.

717
01:01:38.211 --> 01:01:41.130
Well, a lot of guys don't have kills.

718
01:01:41.005 --> 01:01:45.051
And now he's an expert on German
aircraft. When did that happen?

719
01:01:45.384 --> 01:01:48.304
Man, you're scratching fleas
on a stuffed dog.

720
01:01:48.930 --> 01:01:49.972
Nothing there.

721
01:01:50.056 --> 01:01:51.641
Right, we'll see.

722
01:01:51.641 --> 01:01:53.643
Blaine, hey, I'm telling you,

723
01:01:54.226 --> 01:01:56.979
there's something not right with that guy.

724
01:02:04.153 --> 01:02:05.821
Hey, you asleep?

725
01:02:07.156 --> 01:02:08.240
No.

726
01:02:09.241 --> 01:02:10.201
(SIGHS)

727
01:02:10.326 --> 01:02:13.537
A few years ago,
we didn't even have airplanes.

728
01:02:13.746 --> 01:02:15.748
Now there's thousands of us,

729
01:02:15.748 --> 01:02:19.251
with one half trying to kill the other half.

730
01:02:19.251 --> 01:02:21.337
Yeah, that's how it goes.

731
01:02:22.504 --> 01:02:25.007
You really have your own ranch?

732
01:02:25.007 --> 01:02:28.260
I did, 900 acres.

733
01:02:28.677 --> 01:02:31.180
Was in my family for 85 years.

734
01:02:31.764 --> 01:02:33.849
It was a tradition.

735
01:02:33.849 --> 01:02:37.311
Grow up and you work the ranch.

736
01:02:37.311 --> 01:02:38.854
Till my ma left and

737
01:02:40.856 --> 01:02:43.358
my dad died all mortgaged out.

738
01:02:45.360 --> 01:02:48.363
It was kind of hard to make a go of it.

739
01:02:48.363 --> 01:02:52.117
So what you gonna do now?
I mean, when the war is over?

740
01:02:52.034 --> 01:02:53.577
I don't know.

741
01:02:55.454 --> 01:02:58.874
Maybe I'll keep flying
if there's any call for it.

742
01:03:00.959 --> 01:03:02.753
Or get a new ranch.

743
01:03:03.462 --> 01:03:05.047
How about you?

744
01:03:06.089 --> 01:03:07.549
Hard to say.

745
01:03:08.383 --> 01:03:12.054
I came here
'cause I heard they treated Negroes better.

746
01:03:14.139 --> 01:03:16.516
- Do they?
- They were good to me.

747
01:03:18.894 --> 01:03:21.313
I don't wanna go back to boxing.

748
01:03:22.981 --> 01:03:27.360
I'm tired of pounding on people,
keeping my anger up all the time.

749
01:03:29.237 --> 01:03:30.906
And I like flying.

750
01:03:32.157 --> 01:03:36.119
Hell, if you're not fighting,
it's nice and peaceful up there.

751
01:03:37.370 --> 01:03:39.247
Nobody can touch you.

752
01:03:40.290 --> 01:03:43.209
Nobody can make you feel low.

753
01:03:45.920 --> 01:03:49.049
You think there'll be any future
in flying after the war?

754
01:03:49.174 --> 01:03:50.300
Maybe.

755
01:03:52.927 --> 01:03:57.515
I mean, there's always giving people
rides at fairs and things like that.

756
01:03:58.516 --> 01:04:04.272
And I hear they might use planes
to deliver mail from city to city.

757
01:04:04.355 --> 01:04:05.607
Really?

758
01:04:07.275 --> 01:04:11.279
Yeah, I like that.
That'd be a good job for me.

759
01:04:13.364 --> 01:04:17.285
I figure as long as I'm up in the air,
they can't see me,

760
01:04:18.536 --> 01:04:20.872
they won't mind if I'm black.

761
01:04:24.709 --> 01:04:27.211
There's something wrong with Jensen.

762
01:04:27.211 --> 01:04:28.796
BEAGLE: He's down here.

763
01:04:37.722 --> 01:04:38.681
RAWLINGS: Hey?

764
01:04:39.932 --> 01:04:40.892
Hey?

765
01:04:42.018 --> 01:04:43.060
Jensen?

766
01:04:44.228 --> 01:04:45.897
Can you hear me?

767
01:04:46.397 --> 01:04:48.900
- Jensen?
- CASSID Y: Thought this might happen.

768
01:04:49.400 --> 01:04:52.445
Jensen?
You're going through a little shock.

769
01:04:52.653 --> 01:04:53.988
Don't think about flying for a while.

770
01:04:53.988 --> 01:04:55.239
You don't have to go up again
until you're ready.

771
01:04:55.364 --> 01:04:57.033
You understand me?

772
01:04:58.075 --> 01:05:00.244
Do you understand me, Jensen?

773
01:05:04.332 --> 01:05:05.374
(SIGHS)

774
01:05:06.625 --> 01:05:09.336
He tries flying tomorrow, stop him.

775
01:05:10.796 --> 01:05:12.757
CASSID Y: Not that you'll have to.

776
01:05:13.174 --> 01:05:15.926
Meantime, get him some bourbon.

777
01:05:16.427 --> 01:05:19.138
- Go get the bourbon.
- I'll get it.

778
01:05:21.015 --> 01:05:22.600
(WHIMPERING)

779
01:05:33.319 --> 01:05:35.529
(LUCIENNE SPEAKING FRENCH)

780
01:05:39.283 --> 01:05:43.454
- How you are?
- Non, Say, "How are you?"

781
01:05:48.459 --> 01:05:50.002
"How are you?"

782
01:05:50.961 --> 01:05:51.962
(AIRPLANE APPROACHING)

783
01:05:54.047 --> 01:05:56.258
(CHILDREN SPEAKING FRENCH)

784
01:06:11.273 --> 01:06:13.150
(GREETING IN FRENCH)

785
01:06:17.112 --> 01:06:20.032
- How you are?
- How are you?

786
01:06:23.577 --> 01:06:25.036
That's good.

787
01:06:25.036 --> 01:06:28.999
You speak English now.
Then we can have a conversation.

788
01:06:28.915 --> 01:06:30.041
(SPEAKING FRENCH)

789
01:06:30.167 --> 01:06:32.335
Let me hear your English.

790
01:06:34.504 --> 01:06:36.006
Good you see?

791
01:06:37.007 --> 01:06:38.508
Yeah, good.

792
01:06:39.009 --> 01:06:40.760
Good to see you, too.

793
01:06:41.511 --> 01:06:42.846
(SPEAKING FRENCH)

794
01:06:58.124 --> 01:06:59.208
See?

795
01:07:00.751 --> 01:07:03.546
This is my rabbit. Wanna pet it?

796
01:07:03.879 --> 01:07:06.716
Better be gentle. He's jumpy.

797
01:07:09.218 --> 01:07:10.219
(GASPS) Oh.

798
01:07:10.886 --> 01:07:13.889
He looks a little cold.
I think we'll give him a little blanket there.

799
01:07:13.889 --> 01:07:16.809
How's that? There you go.

800
01:07:20.479 --> 01:07:22.022
What about you?

801
01:07:22.440 --> 01:07:24.400
Do you ever have any fun?

802
01:07:24.525 --> 01:07:27.319
(SPEAKING FRENCH)

803
01:07:30.781 --> 01:07:32.032
No time.

804
01:07:32.992 --> 01:07:36.328
No, you're wrong.
Right now's the perfect time.

805
01:07:37.162 --> 01:07:40.249
We don't know how many chances
we're gonna get.

806
01:07:41.000 --> 01:07:44.837
Want to take a ride? In my avion?

807
01:07:45.796 --> 01:07:46.755
- Come on.
- No.

808
01:07:46.922 --> 01:07:48.173
- Come on.
- No.

809
01:09:28.699 --> 01:09:29.784
Here.

810
01:09:31.536 --> 01:09:33.204
(GIGGLING)

811
01:09:37.375 --> 01:09:39.961
Picked a great day to fly, didn't I?

812
01:09:41.629 --> 01:09:43.965
Did you have fun in the air?

813
01:09:43.965 --> 01:09:45.299
(SPEAKING FRENCH)

814
01:09:46.050 --> 01:09:48.302
Fun in the plane?

815
01:09:53.307 --> 01:09:54.266
Okay.

816
01:09:56.560 --> 01:09:58.020
What's this?

817
01:10:00.648 --> 01:10:02.316
"It's not good

818
01:10:03.150 --> 01:10:06.153
"for me to like you."

819
01:10:08.989 --> 01:10:09.990
Why?

820
01:10:11.784 --> 01:10:12.826
(QUESTIONS IN FRENCH)

821
01:10:12.910 --> 01:10:15.829
"Because I worry."

822
01:10:17.748 --> 01:10:19.833
You're worried about me?

823
01:10:35.140 --> 01:10:37.226
(SPEAKING FRENCH)

824
01:10:45.150 --> 01:10:46.193
For me?

825
01:10:47.444 --> 01:10:48.904
From Marie?

826
01:10:50.864 --> 01:10:53.283
Maybe he'll bring me good luck.

827
01:11:04.044 --> 01:11:05.170
Paris?

828
01:11:05.295 --> 01:11:06.963
I've never been.

829
01:11:08.215 --> 01:11:11.635
Maybe you could take me.
Show me all them lights.

830
01:11:19.643 --> 01:11:20.894
Afraid?

831
01:11:22.479 --> 01:11:25.398
- There's a war.
- Am I afraid of the war?

832
01:11:27.984 --> 01:11:29.069
No.

833
01:11:30.195 --> 01:11:31.988
- No?
- No.

834
01:11:35.825 --> 01:11:36.993
Okay.

835
01:11:39.245 --> 01:11:40.205
Yes.

836
01:11:43.541 --> 01:11:45.418
Every time I go up,

837
01:11:46.252 --> 01:11:47.587
I'm afraid.

838
01:12:32.340 --> 01:12:33.591
Rawlings.

839
01:12:35.801 --> 01:12:39.222
- You hear about Beagle?
- No, what?

840
01:12:40.139 --> 01:12:41.933
I went to Thenault about him.

841
01:12:42.058 --> 01:12:45.144
- Why would you do that?
- Thenault had him checked out.

842
01:12:45.061 --> 01:12:47.146
His whole background's all wet laundry.

843
01:12:47.229 --> 01:12:51.108
- PORTER: Everything in his file is made-up.
- They think he's a spy.

844
01:12:55.571 --> 01:12:58.824
Your behavior has raised suspicion
among the men,

845
01:12:58.824 --> 01:13:04.163
and now we discover
that Eddie Beagle is not your real name.

846
01:13:04.246 --> 01:13:07.666
- It's Arthur Becker, huh?
- So I changed my name.

847
01:13:07.583 --> 01:13:09.877
You're from Wisconsin, I see.

848
01:13:11.253 --> 01:13:14.465
There is a very large German population
in Wisconsin

849
01:13:14.340 --> 01:13:16.425
and your name is German.

850
01:13:16.842 --> 01:13:18.219
I'm no spy.

851
01:13:18.344 --> 01:13:23.098
Why didn't you give us your correct name?
Are you a German sympathizer?

852
01:13:24.058 --> 01:13:25.100
No.

853
01:13:25.517 --> 01:13:27.102
We will find out the truth.

854
01:13:27.102 --> 01:13:29.897
- Look, it's not what you think.
- Why not?

855
01:13:33.525 --> 01:13:35.736
We shoot spies, you know.

856
01:13:38.238 --> 01:13:40.240
Sir, may I?

857
01:13:43.368 --> 01:13:44.369
Beagle.

858
01:13:46.788 --> 01:13:49.708
- Come clean.
- I can't.

859
01:13:49.791 --> 01:13:53.045
They're gonna shoot you.
What could be worse than that?

860
01:13:53.045 --> 01:13:56.048
- I swear I'm not a spy.
- I know.

861
01:13:55.964 --> 01:13:59.509
So just tell them what you did
or they're gonna lock you up.

862
01:13:59.509 --> 01:14:01.386
Is that what you want?

863
01:14:08.268 --> 01:14:10.645
I committed a crime back in the States.

864
01:14:12.022 --> 01:14:14.733
- Spit it out, Beagle.
- I robbed a bank.

865
01:14:15.567 --> 01:14:18.487
Hey, I was in debt to a bookie,
and I needed the money.

866
01:14:18.487 --> 01:14:21.323
THENAULT: Was anyone hurt
in the robbery?

867
01:14:21.323 --> 01:14:22.324
No.

868
01:14:22.449 --> 01:14:24.326
How can we be sure?

869
01:14:26.411 --> 01:14:28.496
Because I used a toy gun.

870
01:14:29.539 --> 01:14:30.999
Excuse me?

871
01:14:30.999 --> 01:14:33.585
I used a toy gun. It was all I had.

872
01:14:33.585 --> 01:14:35.253
(MEN SNICKERING)

873
01:14:38.715 --> 01:14:41.217
Can you prove what you're saying?

874
01:14:41.760 --> 01:14:42.761
No.

875
01:14:44.012 --> 01:14:45.263
I can't.

876
01:14:45.805 --> 01:14:46.931
I can.

877
01:14:51.352 --> 01:14:53.938
I saw a discrepancy in his next of kin file

878
01:14:53.938 --> 01:14:56.524
so I sent away for more information,

879
01:14:57.192 --> 01:15:00.695
and I was sent these telegrams
confirming the robbery.

880
01:15:01.863 --> 01:15:04.449
Beagle, in his haste
to escape an armed guard,

881
01:15:04.449 --> 01:15:07.493
dropped most of the money
along with the toy gun.

882
01:15:07.493 --> 01:15:10.830
And although he escaped with only $12.36,

883
01:15:10.830 --> 01:15:12.624
he is guilty of armed robbery

884
01:15:12.624 --> 01:15:14.292
and if he was returned
to the United States,

885
01:15:14.292 --> 01:15:17.211
they would lock him up
for a very, very long time.

886
01:15:17.211 --> 01:15:22.091
The question for us is, can we allow him
to continue flying for the Escadrilles

887
01:15:21.966 --> 01:15:25.553
because we have no legal jurisdiction
in this matter?

888
01:15:27.930 --> 01:15:29.599
It is up to you.

889
01:15:30.141 --> 01:15:31.809
Don't look at me.

890
01:15:32.393 --> 01:15:35.313
Whether he continues to fly is up to them.

891
01:15:35.980 --> 01:15:37.732
It's their squadron.

892
01:15:38.774 --> 01:15:40.860
(RAWLINGS CLEARS THROAT)

893
01:15:41.485 --> 01:15:46.574
Well, I'd like to know what you would have
done if they didn't give you the money.

894
01:15:47.241 --> 01:15:50.161
I don't know. Throw the toy gun at him?

895
01:15:50.161 --> 01:15:53.247
- You probably would have missed.
- LOWRY: Definitely.

896
01:16:04.216 --> 01:16:05.176
Sir?

897
01:16:07.344 --> 01:16:10.055
We don't condone what Beagle's done,

898
01:16:10.890 --> 01:16:13.809
or the horrible way in which he botched it.

899
01:16:14.768 --> 01:16:19.231
But we also don't think he should be
thrown out on stupidity alone.

900
01:16:19.231 --> 01:16:22.359
Although I'd never trust him
with my wallet,

901
01:16:22.359 --> 01:16:26.030
I think we all will continue to trust him
with our lives,

902
01:16:26.447 --> 01:16:30.492
on the off chance that one day
he might actually hit something.

903
01:16:34.371 --> 01:16:35.706
THENAULT: So be it.

904
01:16:58.437 --> 01:17:02.107
Toy gun, huh? That's good. Yeah.

905
01:17:15.203 --> 01:17:18.457
You see, that's why
we have to load our own ammo.

906
01:17:18.331 --> 01:17:21.460
Half these bullets are bent.
Then the guns jam.

907
01:17:21.793 --> 01:17:23.754
They spotted a group of Fokkers.

908
01:17:23.754 --> 01:17:26.173
They're headed towards our infantry
on the road to Rambucourt.

909
01:17:26.173 --> 01:17:27.215
Let's go.

910
01:17:36.933 --> 01:17:38.476
(ALL EX CLAIM)

911
01:17:42.022 --> 01:17:43.481
(SCREAMING)

912
01:17:46.276 --> 01:17:48.278
(SCREAMING)

913
01:17:53.783 --> 01:17:55.160
(GROANING)

914
01:18:09.340 --> 01:18:11.217
(SCREAMING)

915
01:18:29.360 --> 01:18:31.154
(CHEERING)

916
01:18:43.416 --> 01:18:45.418
Yes! Yeah!

917
01:18:46.169 --> 01:18:47.295
Lowry!

918
01:20:10.294 --> 01:20:11.962
(GUN FIRING)

919
01:20:34.359 --> 01:20:35.944
(GROANING)

920
01:21:07.851 --> 01:21:10.895
(MEN SHOUTING IN FRENCH)

921
01:21:10.895 --> 01:21:12.647
(GUNS FIRING)

922
01:21:12.647 --> 01:21:14.649
(SHOUTING IN GERMAN)

923
01:21:16.734 --> 01:21:18.486
(SHOUTING IN FRENCH)

924
01:21:26.494 --> 01:21:28.830
(MAN GROANING)

925
01:21:29.247 --> 01:21:30.999
(GUNS FIRING)

926
01:21:37.463 --> 01:21:39.006
(SCREAMING)

927
01:21:39.966 --> 01:21:41.426
(CHATTERING)

928
01:21:41.426 --> 01:21:42.677
(EXPLOSION)

929
01:22:03.447 --> 01:22:04.865
(MAN SHOUTING)

930
01:22:05.116 --> 01:22:06.867
(GUNS FIRING)

931
01:22:13.749 --> 01:22:15.292
(GROANING)

932
01:22:27.096 --> 01:22:29.181
(MACHINE GUNS FIRING)

933
01:22:35.145 --> 01:22:36.814
(MEN SHOUTING)

934
01:22:53.372 --> 01:22:56.417
- Can you move?
- No, something's pinning my hand.

935
01:22:57.835 --> 01:22:59.336
(GROANING)

936
01:23:03.924 --> 01:23:06.176
Just get out of here, Rawlings!

937
01:23:20.273 --> 01:23:21.441
(YELLS)

938
01:23:27.698 --> 01:23:29.783
(SPEAKING FRENCH)

939
01:23:29.950 --> 01:23:33.286
Hey, come here, come here, come here.
Push the tail up.

940
01:23:33.203 --> 01:23:34.663
Wait. Wait.

941
01:23:35.080 --> 01:23:37.040
(GUNS FIRING)

942
01:23:39.793 --> 01:23:41.753
Okay, push! Push!

943
01:23:41.753 --> 01:23:43.004
(GRUNTING)

944
01:23:47.050 --> 01:23:50.637
- Rawlings, please, just go.
- I'm not gonna leave you.

945
01:23:54.266 --> 01:23:55.642
Just go!

946
01:23:58.436 --> 01:24:00.230
(GRUNTING)

947
01:24:02.399 --> 01:24:04.067
(EXPLOSION)

948
01:24:15.120 --> 01:24:17.080
- What are you doing?
- I'm sorry, Beagle.

949
01:24:17.080 --> 01:24:19.707
No, Rawlings, no!

950
01:24:19.707 --> 01:24:21.167
(SCREAMING)

951
01:24:21.251 --> 01:24:22.502
Get up!

952
01:24:23.586 --> 01:24:25.129
Move! Go!

953
01:24:26.089 --> 01:24:27.507
Go!

954
01:24:38.768 --> 01:24:40.978
(BEAGLE SCREAMING)

955
01:24:44.190 --> 01:24:45.441
BEAGLE: My hand!

956
01:24:45.691 --> 01:24:47.652
(BEAGLE SOBBING)

957
01:24:57.787 --> 01:24:59.330
(CLEARS THROAT)

958
01:25:00.873 --> 01:25:02.667
Mind if I join you?

959
01:25:12.677 --> 01:25:14.053
This is a

960
01:25:14.887 --> 01:25:19.058
100-year-old bottle of Louis XV.
It's incredible.

961
01:25:20.393 --> 01:25:23.229
Would you care to share a glass with me?

962
01:25:23.813 --> 01:25:26.148
This 'cause I saved your life?

963
01:25:26.857 --> 01:25:29.902
No. No, it's because
I've been a pompous ass.

964
01:25:33.113 --> 01:25:34.657
Pour me a glass.

965
01:25:41.455 --> 01:25:42.831
Oh, my.

966
01:25:42.831 --> 01:25:45.417
I stole this from my father's cellar.

967
01:25:45.751 --> 01:25:48.671
If he'd have known, he would probably say

968
01:25:48.754 --> 01:25:52.716
it's the only thing I've ever done
successfully in my life.

969
01:25:53.425 --> 01:25:54.593
Please.

970
01:26:07.940 --> 01:26:09.107
Nice.

971
01:26:10.651 --> 01:26:12.444
I'm glad you like it.

972
01:26:13.570 --> 01:26:16.156
He's gotta be proud you came here.

973
01:26:18.075 --> 01:26:19.201
No.

974
01:26:20.535 --> 01:26:24.331
Actually, it was kind of his idea.

975
01:26:27.751 --> 01:26:32.339
And how many planes you gotta
bring down to get back in his good graces?

976
01:26:32.672 --> 01:26:34.424
Probably just my own.

977
01:26:38.929 --> 01:26:40.889
What does your father do?

978
01:26:42.974 --> 01:26:44.851
My daddy was a slave.

979
01:26:56.655 --> 01:26:58.198
(DOOR CREAKS)

980
01:27:11.127 --> 01:27:13.505
You restless tonight, Rawlings?

981
01:27:16.841 --> 01:27:18.218
Maybe.

982
01:27:20.428 --> 01:27:24.057
- What about you?
- It was a good day.

983
01:27:25.725 --> 01:27:27.393
Not for Wolfert.

984
01:27:29.604 --> 01:27:34.067
- You had no choice but to kill him.
- He had a choice with me.

985
01:27:35.401 --> 01:27:37.695
Yeah, whatever happened in the air
or whatever happened on the ground

986
01:27:37.695 --> 01:27:40.948
with Beagle,
you gotta get that out of your head.

987
01:27:42.408 --> 01:27:43.868
Okay.

988
01:27:44.702 --> 01:27:47.413
Meanwhile, Beagle goes through life
without a hand.

989
01:27:47.413 --> 01:27:50.750
He volunteered for this war.
He knew what he was getting into.

990
01:27:51.709 --> 01:27:54.712
I don't care what happened in the past.
You can't let that affect you.

991
01:27:54.712 --> 01:27:57.548
You got to forget about it.
Otherwise you're a danger to yourself

992
01:27:57.548 --> 01:27:59.634
and everyone else up there.

993
01:28:00.551 --> 01:28:02.637
Do you let go of the past?

994
01:28:03.971 --> 01:28:05.223
(SIGHS)

995
01:28:05.973 --> 01:28:07.016
I...

996
01:28:08.768 --> 01:28:10.686
I heard some things.

997
01:28:14.649 --> 01:28:17.985
- That you lost...
- That I lost my family in a fire?

998
01:28:20.655 --> 01:28:21.822
(CHUCKLES)

999
01:28:21.822 --> 01:28:26.077
No. I didn't fly for Pancho Villa either.

1000
01:28:27.995 --> 01:28:32.041
The truth is, I was a lot like you.

1001
01:28:33.000 --> 01:28:36.003
Full of idealism,
maybe even a sense of honor.

1002
01:28:39.548 --> 01:28:42.885
Then you realize this war
ain't gonna be won by either side.

1003
01:28:43.928 --> 01:28:45.930
Some day it'll just end.

1004
01:28:52.478 --> 01:28:53.729
(SIGHS)

1005
01:28:55.397 --> 01:28:58.734
And everyone will go home,
get on with their lives.

1006
01:29:00.402 --> 01:29:03.322
Tall grass will cover the battlefield.

1007
01:29:05.532 --> 01:29:08.744
And all the pilots we've lost
wouldn't have changed a damn thing.

1008
01:29:13.624 --> 01:29:15.417
Guys like you won't quit.

1009
01:29:16.793 --> 01:29:19.588
So I got to stick around
and try to knock some Huns off your tails,

1010
01:29:19.588 --> 01:29:22.716
and give you a chance to survive
this useless war.

1011
01:29:22.925 --> 01:29:26.386
- That's what you do.
- Not with enough success.

1012
01:29:28.013 --> 01:29:31.141
The guys I started with
are a testament to that.

1013
01:29:33.560 --> 01:29:39.066
Well, if this war is really meaningless,
then why do you fly extra missions?

1014
01:29:39.483 --> 01:29:41.693
Get the ones I've missed.

1015
01:29:43.904 --> 01:29:46.490
Get the ones that killed my friends.

1016
01:29:52.412 --> 01:29:55.332
You got to find your own meaning
in this war.

1017
01:29:56.583 --> 01:30:00.337
I mean, I'll be real disappointed
if we had more pilots die in vain

1018
01:30:00.337 --> 01:30:01.922
than the Germans.

1019
01:30:12.015 --> 01:30:13.808
How many you got left?

1020
01:30:15.602 --> 01:30:16.853
One.

1021
01:30:17.896 --> 01:30:19.439
The Black Falcon.

1022
01:30:19.647 --> 01:30:20.774
(DOOR OPENS)

1023
01:30:31.951 --> 01:30:33.620
(DOG BARKING)

1024
01:30:40.627 --> 01:30:42.462
(VEHICLES APPROACHING)

1025
01:30:44.130 --> 01:30:45.923
(MEN SHOUTING)

1026
01:30:52.055 --> 01:30:56.476
RAWLINGS: See, this whole wing.
Patch on a patch.

1027
01:30:56.476 --> 01:30:58.436
And when they gonna send us
a new canvas?

1028
01:30:58.436 --> 01:31:00.813
- SKINNER: Always "next time."
- Hey, Rawlings.

1029
01:31:00.813 --> 01:31:02.815
The Germans have crossed
the Meuse River.

1030
01:31:02.815 --> 01:31:05.735
And reports say they've overrun Souilly.

1031
01:31:06.152 --> 01:31:07.737
Lucienne.

1032
01:31:08.571 --> 01:31:11.073
Is that plane fuelled? Is this plane fuelled?

1033
01:31:11.073 --> 01:31:12.325
- SKINNER: Rawlings!
- Yes, sir.

1034
01:31:12.325 --> 01:31:14.493
Give me a start. Give me a start. Let's go.

1035
01:31:14.493 --> 01:31:17.496
SKINNER: Rawlings, you know you're
not allowed to take the plane!

1036
01:31:32.094 --> 01:31:33.596
(BANGING ON DOOR)

1037
01:31:33.596 --> 01:31:34.930
(CUP CLATTERS)

1038
01:31:43.481 --> 01:31:45.858
Hey. Hey.

1039
01:31:47.776 --> 01:31:50.446
- You all right? You all right?
- Yeah?

1040
01:31:50.362 --> 01:31:53.365
- How you come?
- My plane. A vion,

1041
01:31:53.699 --> 01:31:55.451
(SPEAKING FRENCH)

1042
01:31:55.451 --> 01:31:58.912
- Germans.
- All right. I'm gonna get you out of here.

1043
01:31:59.747 --> 01:32:01.957
No, it's all right.
I'm gonna get you out of here.

1044
01:32:01.957 --> 01:32:03.500
(SPEAKING IN FRENCH)

1045
01:32:03.917 --> 01:32:06.712
Go get them. Go get them.

1046
01:32:07.463 --> 01:32:09.048
(SPEAKING FRENCH)

1047
01:32:11.008 --> 01:32:15.804
- Lf Rawlings returns alive, arrest him.
- Yes, sir.

1048
01:32:16.555 --> 01:32:18.098
(SPEAKING FRENCH)

1049
01:32:18.640 --> 01:32:21.435
- Good luck.
- Stay right here. Okay?

1050
01:32:21.435 --> 01:32:22.978
You don't go anywhere.
You stay right here.

1051
01:32:22.978 --> 01:32:24.897
(AFFIRMS IN FRENCH)

1052
01:32:32.279 --> 01:32:33.405
(BIDS FAREWELL IN FRENCH)

1053
01:32:33.530 --> 01:32:35.907
RAWLINGS: I'll be back before sunrise.

1054
01:32:43.123 --> 01:32:45.333
(AIRPLANE ENGINE WHIRRING)

1055
01:32:47.085 --> 01:32:48.253
- RAWLINGS: You got her?
- Got them.

1056
01:32:48.336 --> 01:32:49.379
Come on, guys.

1057
01:32:49.379 --> 01:32:52.507
What are you doing flying at night
without authorization?

1058
01:32:52.507 --> 01:32:55.343
I don't have time to explain.
I have to go get one more person.

1059
01:32:55.343 --> 01:32:59.931
This plane is not for your personal use.
Leave this plane and return to quarters.

1060
01:32:59.806 --> 01:33:02.017
- That's an order!
- Yes, sir.

1061
01:33:25.874 --> 01:33:28.376
(MURMURING)

1062
01:33:32.130 --> 01:33:33.381
(CHATTERING)

1063
01:33:38.178 --> 01:33:39.429
(COCKS GUN)

1064
01:33:54.319 --> 01:33:56.237
(SPEAKING GERMAN)

1065
01:34:10.418 --> 01:34:11.669
(GASPS)

1066
01:34:12.378 --> 01:34:14.338
(SOLDIERS CHATTERING
IN GERMAN)

1067
01:34:38.946 --> 01:34:40.448
(TALKING IN GERMAN)

1068
01:35:04.638 --> 01:35:07.224
(SPEAKING GERMAN)

1069
01:36:06.449 --> 01:36:09.035
(SPEAKING GERMAN)

1070
01:36:26.803 --> 01:36:28.555
Freeze!

1071
01:36:28.555 --> 01:36:29.597
(GASPS)

1072
01:36:30.432 --> 01:36:33.643
Hang on, Lucienne. Hang on.

1073
01:36:59.752 --> 01:37:01.838
Monsieur Rawlings.

1074
01:37:08.594 --> 01:37:10.596
(SPEAKING FRENCH)

1075
01:37:14.433 --> 01:37:16.310
Medic!

1076
01:37:19.438 --> 01:37:20.898
Medic!

1077
01:37:24.110 --> 01:37:25.778
MEDIC: Over here, over here.

1078
01:37:25.903 --> 01:37:27.863
(SPEAKING FRENCH)

1079
01:39:09.631 --> 01:39:10.799
Doctor!

1080
01:39:16.638 --> 01:39:18.723
(DOCTOR SPEAKING FRENCH)

1081
01:39:23.520 --> 01:39:26.731
They're taking you
to the hospital at Reims.

1082
01:39:26.731 --> 01:39:28.316
You understand?

1083
01:39:28.400 --> 01:39:30.735
(SPEAKING FRENCH)

1084
01:39:30.735 --> 01:39:33.405
They're right here. They're gonna be fine.

1085
01:39:33.321 --> 01:39:36.032
They contacted your uncle,
and he's gonna take care of them

1086
01:39:36.032 --> 01:39:38.743
until you recover. Okay?

1087
01:39:39.661 --> 01:39:43.957
- Yes. You come?
- Yeah.

1088
01:39:44.791 --> 01:39:48.962
- I'll come see you in Reims.
- Goodbye.

1089
01:39:49.254 --> 01:39:50.630
Okay.

1090
01:39:52.298 --> 01:39:53.341
All right.

1091
01:39:53.550 --> 01:39:55.343
(BIDDING FAREWELL IN FRENCH)

1092
01:40:01.057 --> 01:40:04.185
I have filled out the papers
formally charging you

1093
01:40:04.185 --> 01:40:05.937
with dereliction of duty.

1094
01:40:05.937 --> 01:40:11.609
That sort of thing cannot be tolerated
in a military unit. Not even this one.

1095
01:40:11.901 --> 01:40:16.781
Reports indicate that an Escadrille pilot
flew four French refugees

1096
01:40:16.906 --> 01:40:19.826
out of occupied territory
while being shot at

1097
01:40:19.700 --> 01:40:23.788
by both riflemen and anti-aircraft cannons.

1098
01:40:24.831 --> 01:40:26.207
Busy night.

1099
01:40:26.624 --> 01:40:31.796
I have been in direct communication
with HQ in Paris over your little escapade.

1100
01:40:33.297 --> 01:40:36.300
They agree with
my recommendation completely.

1101
01:40:36.300 --> 01:40:39.720
So it won't do you any good
to go over my head.

1102
01:40:41.639 --> 01:40:44.016
- Take the cuffs off.
- Sir...

1103
01:40:44.016 --> 01:40:47.770
Unless you want to fly his plane.
I think I forgot to sign that.

1104
01:40:47.770 --> 01:40:50.064
Ask me about it again tomorrow.

1105
01:40:54.443 --> 01:40:58.906
Congratulations, Rawlings.
And don't ever do that again.

1106
01:41:09.667 --> 01:41:11.418
I won't, sir.

1107
01:41:27.810 --> 01:41:30.187
THENAULT: Gentlemen,
there is a change of plan.

1108
01:41:30.187 --> 01:41:32.815
We've had a little surprise thrown at us.

1109
01:41:32.815 --> 01:41:36.276
A German zeppelin is on its way
to bomb Paris.

1110
01:41:36.276 --> 01:41:40.531
As you know, our French and British
pilots are engaged at Pont-?Mousson.

1111
01:41:40.447 --> 01:41:46.161
So Rawlings, Lowry, Skinner and Porter
will have to go after the zeppelin.

1112
01:41:46.036 --> 01:41:48.455
Remember to load incendiary bullets.

1113
01:41:48.455 --> 01:41:51.375
It can take hundreds
to bring down a zeppelin.

1114
01:41:51.375 --> 01:41:55.545
The rest of the squadron will support
the others at Pont-?Mousson.

1115
01:41:55.754 --> 01:41:58.882
- May God be with you.
- Thank you, sir.

1116
01:41:58.965 --> 01:42:00.217
Courage.

1117
01:42:01.885 --> 01:42:03.387
- Courage.
- For thine is the kingdom, the power

1118
01:42:03.470 --> 01:42:06.181
and the glory forever and ever. Amen.

1119
01:42:08.141 --> 01:42:09.392
Courage.

1120
01:42:10.143 --> 01:42:11.186
All right.

1121
01:43:03.196 --> 01:43:04.781
(GUNS FIRING)

1122
01:43:36.896 --> 01:43:38.773
(PORTER SINGING HYMN)

1123
01:43:40.524 --> 01:43:41.567
(GROANS)

1124
01:43:45.988 --> 01:43:47.531
(MACHINE GUNS FIRING)

1125
01:44:50.010 --> 01:44:54.264
You go down!
I'll take the zeppelin!

1126
01:45:03.732 --> 01:45:05.317
(GUNS FIRING)

1127
01:45:31.593 --> 01:45:33.053
(SHOUTING)

1128
01:46:45.499 --> 01:46:47.919
(SCREAMING)

1129
01:46:56.260 --> 01:46:57.845
(GASPING)

1130
01:48:06.038 --> 01:48:07.789
No!

1131
01:48:34.566 --> 01:48:36.276
(SPEAKING LATIN)

1132
01:48:41.698 --> 01:48:44.617
- Amen.
- Amen.

1133
01:48:49.497 --> 01:48:54.794
Today we have lost two brave fighters.
Two friends.

1134
01:48:57.630 --> 01:49:03.136
Porter once told me that if he died,
he wanted to be buried by the airfield.

1135
01:49:03.386 --> 01:49:05.638
Near those he fought alongside.

1136
01:49:07.640 --> 01:49:12.437
I'm sure Cassidy would rather be buried
behind the whorehouse.

1137
01:49:12.562 --> 01:49:13.980
(CHUCKLING)

1138
01:49:16.274 --> 01:49:20.361
Only a few days ago,
Cassidy gave me this letter

1139
01:49:20.361 --> 01:49:24.115
to give to Rawlings in the event he died.

1140
01:49:25.283 --> 01:49:27.368
Rawlings, please.

1141
01:49:45.595 --> 01:49:46.929
(CLEARS THROAT)

1142
01:49:48.431 --> 01:49:53.311
"If I do not return,
my burial is of no import.

1143
01:49:55.187 --> 01:49:58.649
"Make it as easy as possible
for yourselves.

1144
01:49:59.150 --> 01:50:02.903
"I have no religion
and do not care for any service.

1145
01:50:04.155 --> 01:50:06.782
"If the omission would bother Porter,

1146
01:50:09.368 --> 01:50:11.662
"I guess I would stand the ceremony.

1147
01:50:13.038 --> 01:50:16.750
"Good luck to you all. Vive la Escadrille,

1148
01:50:16.667 --> 01:50:21.255
"the only real friends I ever had. Cassidy."

1149
01:50:24.466 --> 01:50:27.094
A lot of us owe this man our lives.

1150
01:50:28.137 --> 01:50:29.930
We won't forget him.

1151
01:50:32.641 --> 01:50:34.810
(GIROUX SHOUTING ORDERS
IN FRENCH)

1152
01:50:42.109 --> 01:50:43.569
(GUNS FIRING)

1153
01:50:59.918 --> 01:51:01.420
Sir,

1154
01:51:02.754 --> 01:51:05.674
I made a promise
that I'd meet someone at Reims.

1155
01:51:06.300 --> 01:51:10.345
- Can I have permission to leave the base?
- Yes.

1156
01:51:21.523 --> 01:51:23.400
(PEOPLE CHATTERING)

1157
01:51:38.832 --> 01:51:40.375
Excuse me.

1158
01:51:40.917 --> 01:51:42.168
Sorry.

1159
01:51:43.295 --> 01:51:45.088
Excuse me, I'm looking for...

1160
01:51:49.050 --> 01:51:50.510
Lucienne!

1161
01:51:53.638 --> 01:51:55.432
Lucienne!

1162
01:51:57.183 --> 01:51:59.060
Lucienne!

1163
01:52:04.482 --> 01:52:06.484
(PEOPLE ALL CHATTERING
IN FRENCH)

1164
01:52:19.414 --> 01:52:21.082
RAWLINGS: Lucienne!

1165
01:52:35.138 --> 01:52:37.348
I afraid.

1166
01:52:38.266 --> 01:52:42.019
- Not see you.
- Yeah.

1167
01:52:43.688 --> 01:52:45.481
You look good.

1168
01:52:46.816 --> 01:52:48.776
Yeah. Okay.

1169
01:52:51.195 --> 01:52:53.489
We go to England.

1170
01:52:54.615 --> 01:52:56.534
Not safe for children.

1171
01:52:57.451 --> 01:53:00.079
- Germans come here.
- I know.

1172
01:53:04.041 --> 01:53:07.670
You and me in Paris

1173
01:53:09.338 --> 01:53:10.798
after war?

1174
01:53:11.632 --> 01:53:14.218
Your English is getting so good.

1175
01:53:16.762 --> 01:53:17.888
I try.

1176
01:53:19.056 --> 01:53:22.143
How will I reach you?
I'm gonna be moving.

1177
01:53:26.647 --> 01:53:29.567
I have so much I wanna say to you.

1178
01:53:29.900 --> 01:53:34.989
You will be in my thoughts

1179
01:53:36.657 --> 01:53:39.493
and in my heart.

1180
01:53:46.875 --> 01:53:48.335
(MAN SPEAKING FRENCH)

1181
01:53:51.171 --> 01:53:53.006
(CHILDREN SPEAKING FRENCH)

1182
01:54:11.692 --> 01:54:15.445
I'll see you in Paris.
We'll turn on them lights.

1183
01:54:15.529 --> 01:54:20.033
Be careful.
I will not be here to count the planes.

1184
01:54:20.534 --> 01:54:22.869
(BIDDING FAREWELL IN FRENCH)

1185
01:54:53.733 --> 01:54:56.319
Gentlemen, we are going
to make another run

1186
01:54:56.319 --> 01:54:58.488
on the munition depot at Jametz.

1187
01:54:58.488 --> 01:55:01.241
This time escorting four bombers.

1188
01:55:01.241 --> 01:55:05.829
Instead of a frontal attack,
we fly south to Marcheville first

1189
01:55:05.703 --> 01:55:08.623
and then swing north to the strike area.

1190
01:55:09.582 --> 01:55:13.753
This way, we might be able to surprise
them and get closer to the target

1191
01:55:13.753 --> 01:55:16.422
before encountering resistance.

1192
01:55:16.673 --> 01:55:19.884
As you may have heard,
the United States has just announced

1193
01:55:19.884 --> 01:55:21.970
its entrance into the war.

1194
01:55:21.970 --> 01:55:23.638
- Oh, good.
- Thank God for that.

1195
01:55:23.638 --> 01:55:27.183
I don't need to tell you
that if we destroy Jametz,

1196
01:55:27.183 --> 01:55:31.270
we severely reduce the flow
of ammunition to the German troops.

1197
01:55:31.145 --> 01:55:33.940
Your brothers will be fighting
on the ground.

1198
01:55:34.607 --> 01:55:40.863
I know the last attack on Jametz
was a hard initiation for many of you.

1199
01:55:41.864 --> 01:55:45.618
But I have watched you grow
and develop since then,

1200
01:55:45.535 --> 01:55:48.371
both as men and pilots,

1201
01:55:48.955 --> 01:55:52.208
and I can say that I am proud
to be your captain.

1202
01:55:52.625 --> 01:55:56.170
You have more than exceeded
my expectations.

1203
01:55:56.879 --> 01:55:58.798
Good luck to you all.

1204
01:56:09.100 --> 01:56:11.060
Think you might have dropped that.

1205
01:56:16.065 --> 01:56:18.484
I told her I was gonna be a hero.

1206
01:56:19.652 --> 01:56:20.986
(SIGHS)

1207
01:56:22.863 --> 01:56:26.909
Look, you got nothing to be ashamed of.

1208
01:56:28.828 --> 01:56:33.290
- You went up there and you fought.
- Yeah. Ain't that something?

1209
01:56:33.499 --> 01:56:36.418
Hey, you're gonna be all right.

1210
01:56:37.169 --> 01:56:39.838
- You're already over the jitters.
- Yeah, jitters.

1211
01:56:40.089 --> 01:56:42.883
Yeah. I fixed that.

1212
01:56:47.262 --> 01:56:50.683
I tell Thenault I'm gonna go up again
so he won't send me home,

1213
01:56:50.683 --> 01:56:52.893
but I don't go back up.

1214
01:56:52.893 --> 01:56:57.773
I just watch you guys day after day,
wondering how you do it,

1215
01:56:59.858 --> 01:57:02.611
how everybody in my family did it,

1216
01:57:06.031 --> 01:57:09.368
why I'm the only one who can't.

1217
01:57:11.787 --> 01:57:13.747
All right, come on.

1218
01:57:13.747 --> 01:57:18.335
Why don't you just go?
Go sleep this off and try again tomorrow.

1219
01:57:18.210 --> 01:57:20.712
- Yeah, yeah, tomorrow.
- Okay?

1220
01:57:20.712 --> 01:57:21.797
Okay.

1221
01:57:24.049 --> 01:57:25.300
Okay.

1222
01:57:26.259 --> 01:57:29.596
- We're the knights of the air, remember?
- Yeah.

1223
01:57:31.056 --> 01:57:32.224
MAN: Contact?
SKINNER: Contact.

1224
01:57:37.104 --> 01:57:41.274
Rawlings, requesting permission
to go on this mission, sir.

1225
01:57:41.483 --> 01:57:44.611
- What's that?
- I rigged this up in the machine shop.

1226
01:57:44.611 --> 01:57:47.239
I can fly with it. Tested it out yesterday.

1227
01:57:47.739 --> 01:57:52.118
All right, but if I feel
you're a detriment to the squadron

1228
01:57:52.118 --> 01:57:54.913
and I wave you off, you go right home,
you understand?

1229
01:57:55.038 --> 01:57:57.832
- Perfectly.
- Don't kill yourself on takeoff.

1230
01:57:57.832 --> 01:58:00.251
BEAGLE: Hey, guys, I'm flying!

1231
01:58:09.010 --> 01:58:13.264
Captain Thenault told me I should have it
painted on your plane.

1232
01:58:14.015 --> 01:58:16.017
I hope you don't mind.

1233
01:58:22.982 --> 01:58:24.442
I'm honored.

1234
01:59:35.429 --> 01:59:37.097
(GUNS FIRING)

1235
02:00:21.308 --> 02:00:22.476
Oh, shit.

1236
02:00:43.538 --> 02:00:44.915
(GUN FIRES)

1237
02:01:09.689 --> 02:01:11.274
(GUN FIRING)

1238
02:01:34.005 --> 02:01:36.925
Come on, Eddie, do something right.

1239
02:01:47.226 --> 02:01:50.063
Beware the hook!

1240
02:02:30.019 --> 02:02:31.270
All right!

1241
02:02:54.293 --> 02:02:55.961
(MEN CHATTERING)

1242
02:02:58.047 --> 02:03:02.009
Congratulations, Beagle. Welcome back.

1243
02:03:03.886 --> 02:03:06.305
I wish Lowry had made it here to see this.

1244
02:03:06.305 --> 02:03:07.973
(ENGINE FIRING)

1245
02:03:12.561 --> 02:03:14.521
Where's he going?

1246
02:03:38.503 --> 02:03:39.755
(SHOUTING)

1247
02:05:27.278 --> 02:05:28.612
(GRUNTING)

1248
02:06:01.645 --> 02:06:03.147
(GRUNTING)

1249
02:06:04.982 --> 02:06:06.775
(JENSEN LAUGHING)

1250
02:06:06.984 --> 02:06:10.112
Knights of the air!

1251
02:06:41.268 --> 02:06:43.061
(GUNS FIRING)

1252
02:07:13.216 --> 02:07:14.467
(GASPS)
